{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PdFnpiwPi6SG1WmLsT5f5j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture of all files. Let me now do the renaming systematically. I'll start with the core Elixir library files and work outward. The renaming map is:\n\n- `LiveVue` → `LiveVite` (Elixir module names, TS type names)\n- `live_vue` → `live_vite` (Elixir app name, config keys, file paths)\n- `live-vue` → `live-vite` (kebab-case)\n- `liveVue` → `liveVite` (camelCase in JS/TS)\n- `~VUE` → stays as `~VUE` (this is a Vue sigil, not a LiveVue sigil - it refers to Vue.js)\n- `_live_vue` → `_live_vite` (injection key)\n\nWait - let me reconsider `~VUE`. The sigil `~VUE` is defined in `LiveVue` module as `sigil_VUE`. Since this is a Vue-specific concept (it's a sigil for writing Vue templates), the task says to rename `live_vue`/`LiveVue` references. The `~VUE` sigil name refers to Vue.js itself, not to the library name. I'll leave `~VUE` as-is since it refers to Vue components, not the library name. Same for `.vue` file references.\n\nLet me now do all the Elixir library file renames. I'll use a bash script approach for the bulk content changes, then handle file/directory renames."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24200,"cache_read_input_tokens":60421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24200},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d","uuid":"e9344bac-91ba-4ab3-a65f-929314df1a2f"}
