ever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"f9335d4e-49e5-40b5-a287-9614456f1733\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:36.325Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"0a08cafa-8923-4d8a-b6be-cdbf191d7cbc\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"f9335d4e-49e5-40b5-a287-9614456f1733\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01CAZwoNDxcGWjTLtSMMrVfg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01JcfQ5Ty6R3noFXGM6fhBtq\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/usage-rules.md\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2177,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":11242,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2177},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CY1ZCwyKfx2vhMXJ2Bm5d\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"43f96b76-314e-4564-a595-cd7d4f3bd2c5\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:36.679Z\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"43f96b76-314e-4564-a595-cd7d4f3bd2c5\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"type\":\"progress\",\"data\":{\"type\":\"hook_progress\",\"hookEvent\":\"PostToolUse\",\"hookName\":\"PostToolUse:Read\",\"command\":\"callback\"},\"parentToolUseID\":\"toolu_01JcfQ5Ty6R3noFXGM6fhBtq\",\"toolUseID\":\"toolu_01JcfQ5Ty6R3noFXGM6fhBtq\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:36.681Z\",\"uuid\":\"2a9764d4-05b4-4c00-9ede-db4e2132c1c8\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"43f96b76-314e-4564-a595-cd7d4f3bd2c5\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01JcfQ5Ty6R3noFXGM6fhBtq\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→# LiveVue Usage Rules\\n     2→\\n     3→This document outlines best practices, conventions, and usage patterns for the LiveVue library. Following these guidelines will help you build maintainable, performant applications that leverage Vue.js components within Phoenix LiveView.\\n     4→\\n     5→**Key Principle**: The LiveView holds the source of truth. Vue components are reactive views of server state with their own client-side state.\\n     6→\\n     7→## Component Organization\\n     8→\\n     9→### File Structure\\n    10→\\n    11→**DO** keep Vue components in the `assets/vue` directory. Organize them in a sensible way:\\n    12→\\n    13→```\\n    14→assets/\\n    15→  vue/\\n    16→    index.ts # this is the entry point for the Vue app\\n    17→    components/\\n    18→      ui/\\n    19→        Button.vue\\n    20→        Modal.vue\\n    21→      forms/\\n    22→        ContactForm.vue\\n    23→    pages/\\n    24→      Dashboard.vue\\n    25→    shared/\\n    26→      Layout.vue\\n    27→```\\n    28→\\n    29→### Component Naming\\n    30→\\n    31→**DO** use PascalCase for component file names, longer than a single word:\\n    32→\\n    33→```\\n    34→✅ UserProfile.vue\\n    35→✅ ShoppingCart.vue\\n    36→✅ ContactForm.vue\\n    37→```\\n    38→\\n    39→**DO NOT** use kebab-case or snake_case for file names:\\n    40→\\n    41→```\\n    42→❌ user-profile.vue\\n    43→❌ shopping_cart.vue\\n    44→```\\n    45→\\n    46→**Use** the same name in the `v-component` attribute (match case exactly, without the extension). **Always** pass the socket to the component:\\n    47→\\n    48→```elixir\\n    49→<.vue v-component=\\\"UserProfile\\\" user={@user} v-socket={@socket} />\\n    50→```\\n    51→\\n    52→## Props and Data Flow\\n    53→\\n    54→### Props Passing\\n    55→\\n    56→**DO** pass all necessary data as props from LiveView. Always pass the socket to the component:\\n    57→\\n    58→```elixir\\n    59→<.vue\\n    60→  v-component=\\\"ShoppingCart\\\"\\n    61→  v-socket={@socket}\\n    62→  cartItems={@cart_items}\\n    63→  cartTotal={@cart_total}\\n    64→  currency={@currency}\\n    65→/>\\n    66→```\\n    67→\\n    68→**DO NOT** rely on Vue components to fetch their own data:\\n    69→\\n    70→```vue\\n    71→❌ <!-- WRONG: Fetching data in Vue component -->\\n    72→<script setup>\\n    73→import { onMounted, ref } from 'vue'\\n    74→\\n    75→const items = ref([])\\n    76→\\n    77→onMounted(async () => {\\n    78→  const response = await fetch('/api/cart')\\n    79→  items.value = await response.json()\\n    80→})\\n    81→</script>\\n    82→```\\n    83→\\n    84→### Custom Struct Encoding\\n    85→\\n    86→**DO** implement the `LiveVue.Encoder` protocol for custom structs:\\n    87→\\n    88→```elixir\\n    89→defmodule MyApp.User do\\n    90→  # You can derive the protocol if it doesn't need any customization\\n    91→  @derive {LiveVue.Encoder, only: [:id, :name, :email]}\\n    92→  defstruct [:id, :name, :email, :private_field]\\n    93→end\\n    94→\\n    95→defimpl LiveVue.Encoder, for: MyApp.User do\\n    96→  def encode(user) do\\n    97→    %{\\n    98→      id: user.id,\\n    99→      name: user.name,\\n   100→      email: user.email\\n   101→      # private_field intentionally omitted\\n   102→    }\\n   103→  end\\n   104→end\\n   105→```\\n   106→\\n   107→**DO NOT** pass structs without implementing the encoder protocol:\\n   108→\\n   109→```elixir\\n   110→❌ # This will raise Protocol.UndefinedError\\n   111→<.vue v-component=\\\"UserCard\\\" user={%MyApp.User{}} />\\n   112→```\\n   113→\\n   114→## Event Handling\\n   115→\\n   116→### Phoenix handle_event\\n   117→\\n   118→**Use** Phoenix event handlers for most interactions:\\n   119→\\n   120→```elixir\\n   121→defmodule MyApp.Live.ContactForm do\\n   122→  use LiveVue, :live_view\\n   123→\\n   124→  def handle_event(\\\"like_post\\\", %{\\\"post_id\\\" => post_id}, socket) do\\n   125→    # handle the event here\\n   126→    {:noreply, socket}\\n   127→  end\\n   128→end\\n   129→```\\n   130→\\n   131→### Client-side events\\n   132→\\n   133→**Use** `useLiveVue().pushEvent()` or in the template `$live.pushEvent()` API for dynamic events. `useLiveVue()` and `$live` are the same thing - Vue phoenix hook instance.\\n   134→\\n   135→```vue\\n   136→<script setup>\\n   137→import { useLiveVue } from 'live_vue'\\n   138→\\n   139→const live = useLiveVue()\\n   140→\\n   141→const handleCustomAction = (data) => {\\n   142→  live.pushEvent('custom_action', data)\\n   143→}\\n   144→</script>\\n   145→\\n   146→<template>\\n   147→  <!-- You can also use $live directly in templates -->\\n   148→  <button @click=\\\"$live.pushEvent('simple_action', { value: 'hello' })\\\">\\n   149→    Click me\\n   150→  </button>\\n   151→</template>\\n   152→```\\n   153→\\n   154→**DO** use `useLiveEvent()` for server-to-client communication. It handles component lifecycle correctly.\\n   155→\\n   156→```vue\\n   157→<script setup>\\n   158→import { useLiveEvent } from 'live_vue'\\n   159→\\n   160→useLiveEvent('notification', (data) => {\\n   161→  // Handle server-sent notification\\n   162→  console.log('Received:', data)\\n   163→})\\n   164→</script>\\n   165→```\\n   166→\\n   167→## Server-Side Rendering (SSR)\\n   168→\\n   169→By default, live_vue uses SSR.**DO** disable SSR for components with client-only dependencies:\\n   170→\\n   171→```elixir\\n   172→<.vue\\n   173→  v-component=\\\"ClientOnlyMap\\\"\\n   174→  v-socket={@socket}\\n   175→  v-ssr={false}\\n   176→/>\\n   177→```\\n   178→\\n   179→## Navigation and Routing\\n   180→\\n   181→### Template links supporting LiveView navigation\\n   182→\\n   183→```vue\\n   184→<script setup>\\n   185→import { Link } from 'live_vue'\\n   186→</script>\\n   187→\\n   188→<template>\\n   189→  <!-- Normal link -->\\n   190→  <Link href=\\\"/\\\">Home</Link>\\n   191→  <!-- Navigate to a different route -->\\n   192→  <Link navigate=\\\"/users\\\">Users</Link>\\n   193→  <!-- Patch the current route with different params -->\\n   194→  <Link patch=\\\"/users/3\\\">User 3</Link>\\n   195→  <!-- Patch the current route with query params and replace the history -->\\n   196→  <Link patch=\\\"/users/3?details=true\\\" replace>User 3 with details</Link>\\n   197→</template>\\n   198→```\\n   199→\\n   200→### Navigation Hook\\n   201→\\n   202→**Use** `useLiveNavigation()` for programmatic navigation:\\n   203→\\n   204→```vue\\n   205→<script setup>\\n   206→import { useLiveNavigation } from 'live_vue'\\n   207→\\n   208→const { patch, navigate } = useLiveNavigation()\\n   209→\\n   210→// Same route, different params\\n   211→const updateUser = (user) => patch(`/users/${user.id}`)\\n   212→\\n   213→// Same route, different query params with replace history\\n   214→const goToTab = (tab) => patch({ tab: tab }, { replace: true })\\n   215→\\n   216→// Different route\\n   217→const goToPage = (path) => navigate(path)\\n   218→</script>\\n   219→```\\n   220→\\n   221→**Prefer** `<Link>` components in templates, unless not possible.\\n   222→\\n   223→## File Uploads\\n   224→\\n   225→### Upload Hook\\n   226→\\n   227→**Use** `useLiveUpload()` for file upload functionality. Server-side upload is supported by LiveView in the exact same way as when using HEEX templates.\\n   228→\\n   229→```vue\\n   230→<script setup>\\n   231→import { useLiveUpload } from 'live_vue'\\n   232→\\n   233→const {\\n   234→  entries,\\n   235→  progress,\\n   236→  showFilePicker,\\n   237→  addFiles,\\n   238→  submit,\\n   239→  cancel,\\n   240→  clear,\\n   241→  valid\\n   242→} = useLiveUpload(\\n   243→  () => props.uploadConfig,\\n   244→  {\\n   245→    changeEvent: 'validate_upload',\\n   246→    submitEvent: 'save_upload'\\n   247→  }\\n   248→)\\n   249→</script>\\n   250→```\\n   251→\\n   252→**Use** `addFiles()` for drag-and-drop:\\n   253→\\n   254→```vue\\n   255→<template>\\n   256→  <div\\n   257→    @drop.prevent=\\\"addFiles($event.dataTransfer)\\\"\\n   258→    @dragover.prevent\\n   259→    class=\\\"upload-zone\\\"\\n   260→  >\\n   261→    <p v-if=\\\"entries.length === 0\\\">Drop files here or</p>\\n   262→    <button @click=\\\"showFilePicker\\\">Choose Files</button>\\n   263→\\n   264→    <!-- Show upload progress -->\\n   265→    <div v-if=\\\"entries.length > 0\\\" class=\\\"upload-progress\\\">\\n   266→      <div v-for=\\\"entry in entries\\\" :key=\\\"entry.ref\\\">\\n   267→        {{ entry.client_name }} - {{ entry.progress }}%\\n   268→        <button @click=\\\"cancel(entry.ref)\\\">Cancel</button>\\n   269→      </div>\\n   270→      <p>Overall progress: {{ progress }}%</p>\\n   271→      <p v-if=\\\"!valid\\\" class=\\\"error\\\">Upload has errors</p>\\n   272→    </div>\\n   273→  </div>\\n   274→</template>\\n   275→```\\n   276→\\n   277→## Testing\\n   278→\\n   279→### Component Testing\\n   280→\\n   281→**Test** Vue components through LiveView integration:\\n   282→\\n   283→```elixir\\n   284→test \\\"renders user profile component\\\", %{conn: conn} do\\n   285→  {:ok, view, _html} = live(conn, \\\"/users/1\\\")\\n   286→\\n   287→  # Get Vue component by name or id. Optional if there is only one component on the page.\\n   288→  vue_config = LiveVue.Test.get_vue(view, name: \\\"UserProfile\\\")\\n   289→  # or by ID: vue_config = LiveVue.Test.get_vue(view, id: \\\"user-profile-1\\\")\\n   290→  # or without any arguments: vue_config = LiveVue.Test.get_vue(view)\\n   291→\\n   292→  assert vue_config.props[\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"John Doe\\\"\\n   293→  assert vue_config.props[\\\"email\\\"] == \\\"john@example.com\\\"\\n   294→  assert vue_config.component == \\\"UserProfile\\\"\\n   295→\\n   296→  render_hook(view, \\\"toggle_details\\\", %{\\\"details\\\" => true})\\n   297→\\n   298→  # Details should now be true.\\n   299→  %{props: props} = LiveVue.Test.get_vue(view)\\n   300→  assert props[\\\"details\\\"] == true\\n   301→end\\n   302→```\\n   303→\\n   304→\\n   305→## Troubleshooting\\n   306→\\n   307→Problem: Component is not found on the client side\\n   308→Solution:\\n   309→1. Make sure you use the correct name in the `v-component` attribute (should match file name exactly, without the extension).\\n   310→2. Restart the server to pick up newly created components.\\n   311→3. Ensure resolve function can find that component in `assets/vue/index.ts`.\\n   312→\\n   313→\\n   314→## Forms and Validation\\n   315→\\n   316→### Using useLiveForm Hook\\n   317→\\n   318→**Use** `useLiveForm()` for complex forms with validation, arrays, and nested objects:\\n   319→\\n   320→```vue\\n   321→<script setup>\\n   322→import { Form, useLiveForm } from 'live_vue'\\n   323→\\n   324→type UserForm = {\\n   325→  name: string\\n   326→  email: string\\n   327→  tags: string[]\\n   328→  profile: {\\n   329→    bio: string\\n   330→    skills: Array<{ name: string; level: string }>\\n   331→  }\\n   332→}\\n   333→\\n   334→const props = defineProps<{ form: Form<UserForm> }>()\\n   335→\\n   336→const form = useLiveForm(() => props.form, {\\n   337→  changeEvent: 'validate',     // Event sent on field changes (null to disable)\\n   338→  submitEvent: 'submit',       // Event sent on form submission\\n   339→  debounceInMiliseconds: 300,  // Debounce validation requests\\n   340→  prepareData: (data) => data  // Transform data before sending\\n   341→})\\n   342→\\n   343→// Basic field access\\n   344→const nameField = form.field('name')\\n   345→const emailField = form.field('email')\\n   346→\\n   347→// Nested object fields\\n   348→const bioField = form.field('profile.bio')\\n   349→\\n   350→// Array fields\\n   351→const tagsArray = form.fieldArray('tags')\\n   352→const skillsArray = form.fieldArray('profile.skills')\\n   353→\\n   354→// Nested array fields are also supported\\n   355→const firstSkillNameField = form.field('profile.skills[0].name')\\n   356→\\n   357→// Field operations\\n   358→const addTag = () => tagsArray.add('')\\n   359→const removeTag = (index) => tagsArray.remove(index)\\n   360→</script>\\n   361→\\n   362→<template>\\n   363→  <!-- Basic field with validation -->\\n   364→  <input\\n   365→    v-bind=\\\"nameField.inputAttrs.value\\\"\\n   366→    :class=\\\"{ 'error': nameField.isTouched.value && nameField.errorMessage.value }\\\"\\n   367→  />\\n   368→  <div v-if=\\\"nameField.errorMessage.value\\\">\\n   369→    {{ nameField.errorMessage.value }}\\n   370→  </div>\\n   371→\\n   372→  <!-- Array iteration -->\\n   373→  <div v-for=\\\"(tagField, index) in tagsArray.fields.value\\\" :key=\\\"index\\\">\\n   374→    <input v-bind=\\\"tagField.inputAttrs.value\\\" />\\n   375→    <button @click=\\\"removeTag(index)\\\">Remove</button>\\n   376→  </div>\\n   377→\\n   378→  <!-- Form actions -->\\n   379→  <button @click=\\\"form.submit()\\\" :disabled=\\\"!form.isValid.value\\\">\\n   380→    Submit\\n   381→  </button>\\n   382→  <button @click=\\\"form.reset()\\\">Reset</button>\\n   383→</template>\\n   384→```\\n   385→\\n   386→### Form Field Properties\\n   387→\\n   388→Each field provides reactive state and helpers:\\n   389→\\n   390→```typescript\\n   391→interface FormField<T> {\\n   392→  // Reactive state\\n   393→  value: Ref<T>                    // Current field value\\n   394→  errors: Ref<string[]>            // Validation errors from server\\n   395→  errorMessage: Ref<string>        // First error message\\n   396→  isValid: Ref<boolean>            // No validation errors\\n   397→  isDirty: Ref<boolean>            // Value changed from initial\\n   398→  isTouched: Ref<boolean>          // Field has been interacted with\\n   399→\\n   400→  // Input binding helper (includes value, events, accessibility)\\n   401→  inputAttrs: Ref<{\\n   402→    value: T\\n   403→    onInput: (event: Event) => void\\n   404→    onFocus: () => void\\n   405→    onBlur: () => void\\n   406→    name: string\\n   407→    id: string\\n   408→    'aria-invalid': boolean\\n   409→    'aria-describedby'?: string\\n   410→  }>\\n   411→\\n   412→  // Navigation methods for nested structures\\n   413→  field(key): FormField           // Access nested object field\\n   414→  fieldArray(key): FormFieldArray // Access nested array field\\n   415→}\\n   416→\\n   417→interface FormFieldArray<T> extends FormField<T[]> {\\n   418→  // Array-specific methods\\n   419→  add: (item?: Partial<T>) => void\\n   420→  remove: (index: number) => void\\n   421→  move: (from: number, to: number) => void\\n   422→\\n   423→  // Reactive array of field instances for iteration\\n   424→  fields: Readonly<Ref<FormField<T>[]>>\\n   425→}\\n   426→\\n   427→interface UseLiveFormReturn<T extends object> {\\n   428→  // Form-level state\\n   429→  isValid: Ref<boolean>\\n   430→  isDirty: Ref<boolean>\\n   431→  isTouched: Ref<boolean>\\n   432→  submitCount: Readonly<Ref<number>>\\n   433→  initialValues: Readonly<Ref<T>>\\n   434→\\n   435→  // Type-safe field factory functions\\n   436→  field(key): FormField\\n   437→  fieldArray(key): FormFieldArray\\n   438→\\n   439→  // Form actions\\n   440→  submit: () => Promise<void>\\n   441→  reset: () => void\\n   442→}\\n   443→```\\n   444→\\n   445→### Server-Side Form Setup\\n   446→\\n   447→**Set up** server-side forms in the standard way:\\n   448→\\n   449→```elixir\\n   450→defmodule MyApp.Live.FormTest do\\n   451→  use LiveVue, :live_view\\n   452→\\n   453→  def render(assigns) do\\n   454→    ~H\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   455→    <.vue form={@form} v-component=\\\"UserForm\\\" v-socket={@socket} />\\n   456→    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   457→  end\\n   458→\\n   459→  def mount(params, socket) do\\n   460→    changeset = MyApp.User.changeset(%MyApp.User{}, %{})\\n   461→    socket = assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))\\n   462→    {:ok, socket}\\n   463→  end\\n   464→\\n   465→  def handle_event(\\\"validate\\\", params, socket) do\\n   466→    changeset = MyApp.User.changeset(%MyApp.User{}, params)\\n   467→    {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\\n   468→  end\\n   469→\\n   470→  def handle_event(\\\"submit\\\", params, socket) do\\n   471→    changeset = MyApp.User.changeset(%MyApp.User{}, params)\\n   472→    case Repo.insert(changeset) do\\n   473→      {:ok, _user} ->\\n   474→        {:noreply, socket}\\n   475→      {:error, changeset} ->\\n   476→        {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\\n   477→    end\\n   478→  end\\n   479→end\\n   480→```\\n   481→\\n   482→## Common Anti-Patterns\\n   483→\\n   484→### State Management\\n   485→\\n   486→**DO NOT** use Vue state stores (Pinia, Vuex) for application state:\\n   487→\\n   488→```vue\\n   489→❌ <!-- WRONG: Using Pinia for app state -->\\n   490→<script setup>\\n   491→import { useUserStore } from '@/stores/user'\\n   492→const userStore = useUserStore()\\n   493→</script>\\n   494→```\\n   495→\\n   496→**DO** use LiveView state with reactive props:\\n   497→\\n   498→```elixir\\n   499→✅ <!-- CORRECT: Server-side state -->\\n   500→def handle_event(\\\"update_user\\\", params, socket) do\\n   501→  # Update state on server\\n   502→  {:noreply, assign(socket, user: updated_user)}\\n   503→end\\n   504→```\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"8c669abe-a2ce-4398-aa2a-49dc532cbe5d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:36.681Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"43f96b76-314e-4564-a595-cd7d4f3bd2c5\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"8c669abe-a2ce-4398-aa2a-49dc532cbe5d\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01CAZwoNDxcGWjTLtSMMrVfg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01XdQ5Bp9Fb4Tkm2d8SUdu9B\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/CLAUDE.md\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2177,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":11242,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2177},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CY1ZCwyKfx2vhMXJ2Bm5d\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"9cda80d1-4bb8-402c-8523-c84c49d2e13c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:37.070Z\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"9cda80d1-4bb8-402c-8523-c84c49d2e13c\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"type\":\"progress\",\"data\":{\"type\":\"hook_progress\",\"hookEvent\":\"PostToolUse\",\"hookName\":\"PostToolUse:Read\",\"command\":\"callback\"},\"parentToolUseID\":\"toolu_01XdQ5Bp9Fb4Tkm2d8SUdu9B\",\"toolUseID\":\"toolu_01XdQ5Bp9Fb4Tkm2d8SUdu9B\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:37.073Z\",\"uuid\":\"a35ed312-5dc7-4074-a2da-2cc10f103615\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"9cda80d1-4bb8-402c-8523-c84c49d2e13c\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01XdQ5Bp9Fb4Tkm2d8SUdu9B\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→# LiveVue Library Development\\n     2→\\n     3→Vue.js + Phoenix LiveView integration library. Version 1.0.0.\\n     4→\\n     5→> This is a living document. Claude sessions should update it with brief learnings as they arise. For detailed notes, see [docs/LEARNINGS.md](docs/LEARNINGS.md).\\n     6→\\n     7→## Quick Reference\\n     8→\\n     9→```bash\\n    10→# Tests\\n    11→mix test                          # Elixir tests\\n    12→npm test                          # Vitest (assets/*.test.ts)\\n    13→npm run e2e:test                  # Playwright E2E (test/e2e/)\\n    14→\\n    15→# Setup\\n    16→mix setup                         # First-time setup (deps + npm install)\\n    17→```\\n    18→\\n    19→## Project Structure\\n    20→\\n    21→```\\n    22→lib/\\n    23→├── live_vue.ex              # Main module, ~VUE sigil\\n    24→├── live_vue/components.ex   # <.vue> component, props handling\\n    25→├── live_vue/encoder.ex      # JSON encoding for Vue props\\n    26→├── live_vue/slots.ex        # Slot interoperability\\n    27→└── live_vue/ssr/            # SSR: NodeJS and ViteJS modes\\n    28→assets/\\n    29→├── index.ts                 # Main entry, getHooks()\\n    30→├── hooks.ts                 # Phoenix LiveView hooks\\n    31→├── use.ts                   # Vue composables (useLiveEvent, etc.)\\n    32→├── useLiveForm.ts           # Form handling with Ecto changesets\\n    33→├── jsonPatch.ts             # Efficient prop diffing\\n    34→└── vitePlugin.js            # Vite plugin for component discovery\\n    35→test/e2e/                    # Playwright E2E tests with Phoenix server\\n    36→```\\n    37→\\n    38→## Key Patterns\\n    39→\\n    40→### Component Usage (Elixir)\\n    41→```elixir\\n    42→# In LiveView template\\n    43→<.vue count={@count} v-component=\\\"Counter\\\" v-socket={@socket} />\\n    44→\\n    45→# Or with ~VUE sigil\\n    46→~VUE\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    47→<Counter :count=\\\"count\\\" />\\n    48→\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    49→```\\n    50→\\n    51→### Vue Composables (TypeScript)\\n    52→- `useLiveVue()` - Access to `$live.pushEvent()`, props\\n    53→- `useLiveEvent(name, handler)` - LiveView event subscription\\n    54→- `useLiveNavigation()` - `patch()` and `navigate()` helpers\\n    55→- `useLiveForm(formName)` - Server-side validation with Ecto\\n    56→- `useLiveUpload(uploadName)` - File upload integration\\n    57→\\n    58→### SSR Modes\\n    59→- `LiveVue.SSR.NodeJS` - Node.js subprocess (default)\\n    60→- `LiveVue.SSR.ViteJS` - HTTP to Vite dev server (dev mode)\\n    61→\\n    62→## E2E Testing\\n    63→\\n    64→Colocated feature structure in `test/e2e/features/`:\\n    65→\\n    66→```\\n    67→test/e2e/features/\\n    68→├── basic/            # Each feature is a directory\\n    69→│   ├── live.ex       # LiveView module\\n    70→│   ├── counter.vue   # Vue component(s)\\n    71→│   └── basic.spec.js # Playwright test\\n    72→├── form/\\n    73→├── stream/\\n    74→└── ...\\n    75→```\\n    76→\\n    77→To add a new E2E test:\\n    78→1. Create `test/e2e/features/my-feature/`\\n    79→2. Add `live.ex` (LiveView), `*.vue` (components), `*.spec.js` (test)\\n    80→3. Add route to `test/e2e/test_helper.exs` router\\n    81→\\n    82→Key utilities in `test/e2e/utils.js`:\\n    83→- `syncLV(page)` - Wait for LiveView connection\\n    84→- `evalLV(page, code)` - Execute Elixir in LiveView process\\n    85→\\n    86→## Conventions\\n    87→\\n    88→Commit format: `type: description` (feat/fix/docs/test/refactor/chore)\\n    89→\\n    90→## Release Process\\n    91→\\n    92→No JS build step required. `package.json` exports point directly to TypeScript source files (`assets/*.ts`). Vite handles TS transpilation when consumers bundle their app.\\n    93→\\n    94→For hex.pm releases, `mix release.{patch,minor,major}` runs easy_publish (bumps version, updates CHANGELOG, commits, tags, pushes, publishes to Hex).\\n    95→\\n    96→## Reference Projects\\n    97→\\n    98→- **React examples**: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro` — Use this Astro project as a reference when you need React component examples or patterns (e.g., for comparing React vs Vue approaches, porting features, or understanding equivalent React implementations).\\n    99→\\n   100→## Notes\\n   101→\\n   102→- This is a library - use E2E tests (`npm run e2e:test`) for testing\\n   103→- CI: Elixir (.github/workflows/elixir.yml), Frontend (.github/workflows/frontend.yml)\\n   104→\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"61a58776-382d-4273-b3c8-9189226ffffe\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:37.072Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"9cda80d1-4bb8-402c-8523-c84c49d2e13c\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"61a58776-382d-4273-b3c8-9189226ffffe\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01CAZwoNDxcGWjTLtSMMrVfg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01V7HkaTLCo7HFCASsJ7ivqw\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/README.md\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2177,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":11242,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2177},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CY1ZCwyKfx2vhMXJ2Bm5d\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"6377a1cc-1ff7-4fcb-9740-dabc1d75a178\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:37.410Z\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"6377a1cc-1ff7-4fcb-9740-dabc1d75a178\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"type\":\"progress\",\"data\":{\"type\":\"hook_progress\",\"hookEvent\":\"PostToolUse\",\"hookName\":\"PostToolUse:Read\",\"command\":\"callback\"},\"parentToolUseID\":\"toolu_01V7HkaTLCo7HFCASsJ7ivqw\",\"toolUseID\":\"toolu_01V7HkaTLCo7HFCASsJ7ivqw\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:37.412Z\",\"uuid\":\"e7d49746-2718-4fd6-944b-f6e9e971e556\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"6377a1cc-1ff7-4fcb-9740-dabc1d75a178\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01V7HkaTLCo7HFCASsJ7ivqw\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→<div align=\\\"center\\\">\\n     2→    <img src=\\\"https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/blob/main/live_vue_logo_rounded.png?raw=true\\\" alt=\\\"Description\\\" height=\\\"256px\\\">\\n     3→<br>\\n     4→<a href=\\\"https://hex.pm/packages/live_vue\\\"><img src=\\\"https://img.shields.io/hexpm/v/live_vue.svg\\\" alt=\\\"Hex.pm\\\"></a>\\n     5→<a href=\\\"https://hexdocs.pm/live_vue\\\"><img src=\\\"https://img.shields.io/badge/docs-hexdocs.pm-purple\\\" alt=\\\"Hexdocs.pm\\\"></a>\\n     6→<a href=\\\"https://github.com/Valian/live_vue\\\"><img src=\\\"https://img.shields.io/github/stars/Valian/live_vue?style=social\\\" alt=\\\"GitHub\\\"></a>\\n     7→<br><br>\\n     8→Vue inside Phoenix LiveView with seamless end-to-end reactivity.\\n     9→</div>\\n    10→\\n    11→## Features\\n    12→\\n    13→-   ⚡ **End-To-End Reactivity** with LiveView\\n    14→-   🧙‍♂️ **One-line Install** - Automated setup via Igniter installer\\n    15→-   🔋 **Server-Side Rendered** (SSR) Vue\\n    16→-   🐌 **Lazy-loading** Vue Components\\n    17→-   📦 **Efficient Props Diffing** - Only changed data is sent over WebSocket\\n    18→-   🪄 **~VUE Sigil** as an alternative LiveView DSL with VS Code syntax highlighting\\n    19→-   🎯 **Phoenix Streams** Support with efficient patches\\n    20→-   🦄 **Tailwind** Support\\n    21→-   🦥 **Slot Interoperability**\\n    22→-   📁 **File Upload Composable** - `useLiveUpload()` for seamless Vue integration with LiveView uploads\\n    23→-   📝 **Comprehensive Form Handling** - `useLiveForm()` with server-side validation via Ecto changesets\\n    24→-   🚀 **Amazing DX** with Vite\\n    25→\\n    26→\\n    27→## Resources\\n    28→\\n    29→-   [Live Examples](https://livevue.skalecki.dev) - Interactive demos\\n    30→-   [HexDocs](https://hexdocs.pm/live_vue)\\n    31→-   [HexPackage](https://hex.pm/packages/live_vue)\\n    32→-   [Phoenix LiveView](https://github.com/phoenixframework/phoenix_live_view)\\n    33→\\n    34→## Example\\n    35→\\n    36→After installation, you can use Vue components in the same way as you'd use functional LiveView components. You can even handle Vue events with `JS` hooks! All the `phx-click`, `phx-change` attributes works inside Vue components as well.\\n    37→\\n    38→```html\\n    39→<script setup lang=\\\"ts\\\">\\n    40→import {ref} from \\\"vue\\\"\\n    41→\\n    42→// props are passed from LiveView\\n    43→const props = defineProps<{count: number}>()\\n    44→\\n    45→// local state\\n    46→const diff = ref(1)\\n    47→</script>\\n    48→\\n    49→<template>\\n    50→  Current count: {{ props.count }}\\n    51→  <label>Diff: </label>\\n    52→  <input v-model.number=\\\"diff\\\" type=\\\"range\\\" min=\\\"1\\\" max=\\\"10\\\" />\\n    53→\\n    54→  <button phx-click=\\\"inc\\\" :phx-value-diff=\\\"diff\\\">\\n    55→    Increase counter by {{ diff }}\\n    56→  </button>\\n    57→</template>\\n    58→```\\n    59→\\n    60→```elixir\\n    61→defmodule MyAppWeb.CounterLive do\\n    62→  use MyAppWeb, :live_view\\n    63→\\n    64→  def render(assigns) do\\n    65→    ~H\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    66→    <.vue count={@count} v-component=\\\"Counter\\\" v-socket={@socket} />\\n    67→    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    68→  end\\n    69→\\n    70→  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\\n    71→    {:ok, assign(socket, count: 0)}\\n    72→  end\\n    73→\\n    74→  def handle_event(\\\"inc\\\", %{\\\"diff\\\" => value}, socket) do\\n    75→    {:noreply, update(socket, :count, &(&1 + value))}\\n    76→  end\\n    77→end\\n    78→```\\n    79→\\n    80→## Why?\\n    81→\\n    82→Phoenix Live View makes it possible to create rich, interactive web apps without writing JS.\\n    83→\\n    84→But once you'll need to do anything even slightly complex on the client-side, you'll end up writing lots of imperative, hard-to-maintain hooks.\\n    85→\\n    86→LiveVue allows to create hybrid apps, where part of the session state is on the server and part on the client.\\n    87→\\n    88→### Reasons why you'd like to use LiveVue\\n    89→\\n    90→-   Your hooks are starting to look like jQuery\\n    91→-   You have a complex local state\\n    92→-   You'd like to use a massive Vue ecosystem\\n    93→-   You want transitions, graphs etc.\\n    94→-   You simply like Vue 😉\\n    95→\\n    96→## Installation\\n    97→\\n    98→**New project:**\\n    99→```bash\\n   100→mix archive.install hex igniter_new\\n   101→mix igniter.new my_app --with phx.new --install live_vue\\n   102→```\\n   103→\\n   104→**Existing project (Phoenix 1.8+ only):**\\n   105→```bash\\n   106→mix igniter.install live_vue\\n   107→```\\n   108→\\n   109→Igniter installer works only for Phoenix 1.8+ projects. For detailed installation instructions, see the [Installation Guide](guides/installation.md).\\n   110→\\n   111→## VS Code Extension\\n   112→\\n   113→For syntax highlighting of the `~VUE` sigil:\\n   114→- **VS Code Marketplace**: Install [LiveVue](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=guilhermepsf23.livevue-sigil-highlighting) extension\\n   115→- **Manual Installation**: Download VSIX from [releases](https://github.com/GuilhermePSF/live-vue-sigil-highlighting/releases) and install via `Extensions > Install from VSIX...`\\n   116→\\n   117→## Guides\\n   118→\\n   119→### Getting Started\\n   120→ - [Getting Started](guides/getting_started.md) - Create your first Vue component with transitions\\n   121→\\n   122→### Core Usage\\n   123→ - [Basic Usage](guides/basic_usage.md) - Fundamental patterns, ~VUE sigil, and common examples\\n   124→ - [Forms and Validation](guides/forms.md) - Complex forms with server-side validation using useLiveForm\\n   125→ - [Configuration](guides/configuration.md) - Advanced setup, SSR, and customization options\\n   126→\\n   127→### Reference\\n   128→ - [Component Reference](guides/component_reference.md) - Complete syntax documentation\\n   129→ - [Client-Side API](guides/client_api.md) - Vue composables and utilities\\n   130→\\n   131→### Advanced Topics\\n   132→ - [Architecture](guides/architecture.md) - How LiveVue works under the hood\\n   133→ - [Testing](guides/testing.md) - Testing Vue components in LiveView\\n   134→ - [Deployment](guides/deployment.md) - Production deployment guide\\n   135→\\n   136→### Help & Troubleshooting\\n   137→ - [FAQ](guides/faq.md) - Common questions and comparisons\\n   138→ - [Troubleshooting](guides/troubleshooting.md) - Debug common issues\\n   139→ - [Comparison](guides/comparison.md) - LiveVue vs other solutions\\n   140→\\n   141→## Relation to LiveSvelte\\n   142→\\n   143→This project is heavily inspired by ✨ [LiveSvelte](https://github.com/woutdp/live_svelte) ✨. Both projects try to solve the same problem. LiveVue was started as a fork of LiveSvelte with adjusted ESbuild settings, and evolved to use Vite and a slightly different syntax. I strongly believe more options are always better, and since I love Vue and it's ecosystem I've decided to give it a go 😉\\n   144→\\n   145→You can read more about differences between Vue and Svelte [in FAQ](guides/faq.md#how-does-livevue-compare-to-livesvelte) or [in comparison guide](guides/comparison.md).\\n   146→\\n   147→## LiveVue Development\\n   148→\\n   149→### Local Setup\\n   150→\\n   151→Ensure you have Node.js installed. Clone the repo and run `mix setup`.\\n   152→\\n   153→No build step is required for the library itself - Vite handles TypeScript transpilation when consumers bundle their app.\\n   154→\\n   155→Use `npm run e2e:test` to run the Playwright E2E tests.\\n   156→\\n   157→### Testing Local Changes in Another Project\\n   158→\\n   159→To test local LiveVue changes in a separate Phoenix project, use a path dependency in your project's `mix.exs`:\\n   160→\\n   161→```elixir\\n   162→{:live_vue, path: \\\"../live_vue\\\"}\\n   163→```\\n   164→\\n   165→Then run `mix deps.get && npm install`. The installer already configures `package.json` to use `file:./deps/live_vue`, so both Elixir and npm will point to your local copy.\\n   166→\\n   167→Elixir changes are reflected immediately. For TypeScript changes, run `npm install` again to pick them up.\\n   168→\\n   169→### Releasing\\n   170→\\n   171→Release is done with `expublish` package.\\n   172→\\n   173→-   Write version changelog in untracked `RELEASE.md` file\\n   174→-   Update version in `INSTALLATION.md`\\n   175→\\n   176→Run\\n   177→\\n   178→```bash\\n   179→git add INSTALLATION.md\\n   180→git commit -m \\\"INSTALLATION version bump\\\"\\n   181→\\n   182→# to ensure everything works fine\\n   183→mix expublish.minor --dry-run --allow-untracked --branch=main\\n   184→\\n   185→# to publish\\n   186→mix expublish.minor --allow-untracked --branch=main\\n   187→```\\n   188→\\n   189→## Features Implemented 🎯\\n   190→\\n   191→- [x] `useLiveEvent` - automatically attaching & detaching [`handleEvent`](https://hexdocs.pm/phoenix_live_view/js-interop.html#client-hooks-via-phx-hook)\\n   192→- [x] JSON Patch diffing - send only changed props over the WebSocket\\n   193→- [x] VS Code extension - syntax highlighting for `~VUE` sigil\\n   194→- [x] Igniter installer - one-line installation for Phoenix 1.8+ projects\\n   195→- [x] `useEventReply` - easy handling of `{:reply, data, socket}` responses\\n   196→- [x] `useLiveForm` - Ecto changesets & server-side validation\\n   197→- [x] Phoenix Streams - full support for `stream()` operations\\n   198→\\n   199→## Credits\\n   200→\\n   201→[LiveSvelte](https://github.com/woutdp/live_svelte)\\n   202→\\n   203→## Star History\\n   204→\\n   205→[![Star History Chart](https://api.star-history.com/svg?repos=Valian/live_vue&type=Date)](https://star-history.com/#Valian/live_vue&Date)\\n   206→\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"81dda4c5-89a4-41ba-bfe3-9015df61d231\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:37.412Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"6377a1cc-1ff7-4fcb-9740-dabc1d75a178\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"81dda4c5-89a4-41ba-bfe3-9015df61d231\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01E8rNRbD6bvLtstGvK1YKKw\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now I have the contents of all six files. Let me create a task list and start editing.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":11683,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":13419,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":11683},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CY1ZDL5rLpphjjwYC6EjG\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"4a819b19-19c6-4a68-b55f-dff15225a542\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-11T03:16:40.758Z\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"4a819b19-19c6-4a68-b55f-dff15225a542\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue\",\"sessionId\":\"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d\",\"version\":\"2.1.32\",\"gitBranch\":\"main\",\"agentId\":\"a030e44\",\"slug\":\"ticklish-crafting-duckling\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01E8rNRbD6bvLtstGvK1YKKw\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_013fb19dxv1kam8Aqv3KJb9g\",\"name\":\"TodoWrite\",\"input\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Edit .git