{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015mQRtVwG77QQuU3TCjQxZw","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Changelog\n     2→\n     3→All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n     4→\n     5→The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),\n     6→and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\n     7→\n     8→<!-- %% CHANGELOG_ENTRIES %% -->\n     9→\n    10→## 1.0.0 - 2026-01-06\n    11→\n    12→After over four months of release candidates and community feedback, LiveVue 1.0 is ready. This release brings a complete rewrite of the developer experience—from a simplified no-build-step architecture to powerful new composables for forms, file uploads, and real-time communication. Whether you're building interactive dashboards, complex forms with server-side validation, or real-time collaborative features, LiveVue now provides first-class tooling to make Vue and Phoenix LiveView work together seamlessly.\n    13→\n    14→### Breaking Changes\n    15→\n    16→- **Removed `shared_props` configuration** - This feature had a fundamental flaw: LiveView only re-renders components when explicitly-passed assigns change. Since shared props were injected at render time (not in the template), changes to shared props would not trigger component re-renders. Pass props explicitly instead: `<.vue flash={@flash} user={@current_user} ... />`\n    17→- **Renamed `nillify_not_loaded` to `nilify_not_loaded` in `LiveVue.Encoder`**. It was a typo and the new spelling is consistent with rest of the Elixir ecosystem.\n    18→\n    19→### Features\n    20→\n    21→- **`useLiveForm` composable** - Comprehensive form handling with server-side validation, nested objects, and dynamic arrays\n    22→- **`useEventReply` composable** - Reactive bi-directional LiveView event communication with server responses\n    23→- **`useLiveConnection` composable** - Reactive WebSocket connectivity monitoring for connection status indicators and offline handling\n    24→- **Phoenix Streams support** - Full integration with LiveView streams for efficient list rendering\n    25→- **Phoenix AsyncResult support** - `assign_async` works correctly out of the box when passed as a prop\n    26→- **Igniter-based installer** - Run `mix igniter.install live_vue` for automated project setup\n    27→\n    28→### Improvements\n    29→\n    30→- **No JavaScript build step** - Package exports TypeScript source files directly; Vite handles transpilation during your app's build\n    31→- **Flattened assets structure** - Simpler `assets/` directory layout\n    32→- **Improved component lookup** - More flexible matching for `findComponent`\n    33→- **LazyHTML for testing** - Replaced Floki with LazyHTML for lighter testing utilities\n    34→- **Elixir 1.19 and OTP 28 support**\n    35→- **VS Code extension** - Syntax highlighting for Vue sigils (`~VUE`)\n    36→- **AGENTS.md integration** - Installation appends LiveVue usage rules for AI-assisted development\n    37→\n    38→### Bug Fixes\n    39→\n    40→- Fixed slots containing non-ASCII characters not displaying correctly\n    41→- Fixed diff values not always being correctly encoded\n    42→- Fixed removal of embedded items in forms\n    43→- Fixed streams handling when `enable_props_diff: false`\n    44→- Fixed stream items inserted at index 0 appearing in wrong order\n    45→- Fixed SSR bundle overwriting client bundle files\n    46→- Fixed encoder compilation without Ecto dependency\n    47→- Fixed installer skipping html_helpers modification for LiveVue-prefixed projects\n    48→- Exported `useField` and `useArrayField` from `useLiveForm.ts`\n    49→\n    50→## 1.0.0-rc.4 - 2025-10-19\n    51→\n    52→### Improvements\n    53→\n    54→- Added support for Elixir 1.19 and OTP 28\n    55→\n    56→### Bug Fixes\n    57→\n    58→- Fixed a bug when [diff values were not always correctly encoded](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/commit/56fe9956d9144950ed3460f0412250a112f25f80)\n    59→- Fixed a bug with [removal of embedded items in the form](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/commit/140e060ddf80bef4c20a12ce6ebe332c9ad321b8)\n    60→\n    61→\n    62→## 1.0.0-rc.3 - 2025-10-01\n    63→\n    64→### Improvements\n    65→\n    66→- Replaced Floki with LazyHTML for testing utilities [#92](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/92)\n    67→\n    68→### Bug Fixes\n    69→\n    70→- Streams work correctly when using diff is disabled [#91](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/91)\n    71→\n    72→\n    73→## 1.0.0-rc.2 - 2025-09-28\n    74→\n    75→### Improvements\n    76→\n    77→- Added usage rules to AGENTS.md file when running `mix live_vue.install` [#87](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/87)\n    78→- Added installation instructions about LiveVue VS code extension to README.md [#86](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/86)\n    79→\n    80→\n    81→### Bug Fixes\n    82→\n    83→- Exporting useField and useArrayField from useLiveForm.ts [#81](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/81)\n    84→- When inserting items at index 0 of stream, the items were not inserted in the correct order\n    85→- Fixed bug when building SSR bundle overriden files from client bundle in priv/static\n    86→\n    87→\n    88→\n    89→## 1.0.0-rc - 2025-09-03\n    90→\n    91→### Features\n    92→\n    93→- **New `useLiveForm` Composable**: Added comprehensive form handling with server-side validation, nested objects, and dynamic arrays [#70](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/70)\n    94→- **New `useEventReply` Composable**: Added reactive composable for bi-directional LiveView event communication with server responses [#75](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/75)\n    95→- **New `useLiveConnection` Composable**: Added reactive WebSocket connectivity monitoring for connection status indicators and offline handling [#76](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/76)\n    96→- added support for **Phoenix Streams** [#72](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/72)\n    97→- added support for **Phoenix AsyncResult** - `assign_async` should work correctly out of the box when passed as a prop. On the Vue side, it can be typed as [#77](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/77)\n    98→- added support for **shared props** - props that are shared between all components [#78](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/71)\n    99→\n   100→### Improvements\n   101→\n   102→- aded Igniter installer instead of a lengthy manual installation process [#73](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/73)\n   103→- added `usage-rules.md` to help with AI-assisted development using LiveVue\n   104→\n   105→\n   106→## 0.7.3 - 2025-08-18\n   107→\n   108→### Improvements\n   109→\n   110→- Added fallback type definitions for phoenix_live_view versions < 1.1 that don't export TypeScript types\n   111→- Enhanced type compatibility with conditional DOM types that adapt to server vs client environments\n   112→- Improved TypeScript development experience with better type safety across different phoenix_live_view versions\n   113→\n   114→\n   115→## 0.7.2 - 2025-08-12\n   116→\n   117→### Improvements\n   118→\n   119→- Docs links are now working in both Github and docs [#66](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/66)\n   120→\n   121→### Bug fixes\n   122→\n   123→- Types for `$live` should now be correctly resolved\n   124→\n   125→\n   126→## 0.7.1 - 2025-07-30\n   127→\n   128→### 🐛 Bugfixes\n   129→\n   130→- Fixed `useLiveUpload` composable to properly handle change event dispatching for `addFiles` - now auto uploads for drag and drop should be working\n   131→- `addFiles` now accepts `DataTransfer` objects directly\n   132→- diff algorithm correctly handles time and date values - they're maps internally, but should be diffed as strings.\n   133→\n   134→### 🧪 Testing\n   135→\n   136→- Added E2E tests for drag and drop functionality\n   137→\n   138→\n   139→## 0.7.0 - 2025-07-29\n   140→\n   141→### 🚀 New Composable: useLiveUpload\n   142→\n   143→- **File Upload Composable**: Added `useLiveUpload()` composable for seamless Vue integration with Phoenix LiveView file uploads\n   144→  - Provides reactive upload state management with progress tracking and metadata\n   145→  - Automatic DOM element management for file inputs\n   146→  - Built-in support for drag-and-drop file handling\n   147→  - Integration with LiveView's upload validation and submission system\n   148→  - TypeScript support with full type definitions for upload configurations\n   149→  - Simplifies complex upload workflows with a declarative Vue-friendly API\n   150→\n   151→### 🧪 Testing Improvements\n   152→\n   153→- **Frontend Test Suite**: Added comprehensive test suite for frontend TypeScript code using Vitest framework\n   154→  - Tests for JSON Patch functionality (`assets/js/live_vue/jsonPatch.ts`) with 36 test cases covering all operations\n   155→  - Test configuration with jsdom environment for DOM testing\n   156→  - Coverage includes edge cases like escaped characters, deep cloning, and complex patch sequences\n   157→- **End-to-End Test Suite**: Added comprehensive E2E test suite using Playwright framework ([#64](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/64))\n   158→  - Tests for Vue component rendering, props passing, event emission, and LiveView/Vue synchronization\n   159→  - 5 test suites covering basic functionality, navigation, events, prop diffs, and file uploads\n   160→  - Test server setup with dedicated Phoenix endpoint for isolated testing\n   161→  - Utilities for LiveView/Vue synchronization and server-side code execution\n   162→- **Separate CI Workflows**: Split testing into dedicated workflows for better separation of concerns\n   163→  - **Frontend CI**: Tests TypeScript code across Node.js versions 20, 22, and 24 (LTS and current stable)\n   164→  - **Elixir CI**: Focused purely on Elixir/OTP matrix testing without redundant frontend test runs\n   165→- **New Mix Commands**: Added `mix assets.test` alias for running frontend tests alongside existing npm scripts\n   166→  - `npm test` - Run tests once\n   167→  - `npm run test:watch` - Run tests in watch mode\n   168→  - `npm run test:ui` - Run tests with interactive UI\n   169→  - `npm run e2e:test` - Run E2E tests\n   170→  - `npm run e2e:test:headed` - Run E2E tests with browser UI\n   171→  - `npm run e2e:test:debug` - Run E2E tests in debug mode\n   172→\n   173→\n   174→## 0.6.1 - 2025-07-24\n   175→\n   176→### Fixes 🐛\n   177→\n   178→- correctly encode props in SSR mode\n   179→- correctly handle diffs for nil values in props\n   180→- added package version to the package.json\n   181→\n   182→## 0.6.0 - 2025-07-22\n   183→\n   184→### ✨ Features and Improvements\n   185→\n   186→*   **JSON Patch Diffs for Props**: LiveVue now uses JSON Patch operations to send only the minimal differences when props change, dramatically reducing WebSocket payload sizes. Instead of sending entire prop objects, only the specific fields that changed are transmitted using RFC 6902 JSON Patch format. This optimization works seamlessly with complex nested structures, lists, and custom structs through the `LiveVue.Encoder` protocol. It's possible to skip diffs by setting `v-diff` to `false` on the component or by setting `config :live_vue, enable_props_diff: false` in your config. ([#60](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/60))\n   187→*   **New `useLiveNavigation` Composable**: A new `useLiveNavigation` composable has been added for programmatic navigation, mirroring the functionality of `live_patch` and `live_redirect`. ([#59](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/59)).\n   188→*   **New `useLiveEvent` Composable**: A new `useLiveEvent` composable has been added to simplify listening to server-pushed events. It automatically manages event listener lifecycle, reducing boilerplate and preventing memory leaks ([#58](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/58)).\n   189→*   **New `Link` Component**: A new `<Link>` Vue component has been added to simplify `live_patch` and `live_redirect` navigation within your Vue components. ([#47](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/47)).\n   190→*   **TypeScript by Default**: The client-side entrypoint at `assets/vue/index.ts` is now a TypeScript file by default, improving type safety and the development experience out of the box.\n   191→*   **`$live` Template Property**: The LiveView hook instance is now automatically available in all Vue templates as the `$live` property, providing a convenient alternative to `useLiveVue()`. The property is now also fully typed, providing autocompletion and type checking in your editor. ([#56](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/56)).\n   192→*   **Documentation Overhaul**: The documentation has been completely rewritten and expanded. It now includes comprehensive guides on architecture, basic and advanced usage, a full client-side API reference, a component reference, and much more. ([#49](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/49))\n   193→*   **Testing Utilities**: The new `LiveVue.Test` module provides helpers to inspect Vue component configuration (props, slots, event handlers) within your LiveView tests, making it easier to write assertions. ([#46](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/46))\n   194→*   **GitHub CI**: A new GitHub Actions workflow has been added to run tests automatically.\n   195→\n   196→### ⬆️ Migration Guide\n   197→\n   198→This version transitions the default client-side setup to TypeScript and renames ~V sigil to ~VUE. If you have an existing `assets/vue/index.js`, follow these steps to upgrade:\n   199→\n   200→1.  **Rename and replace `index.js`**:\n   201→    *   Delete your existing `assets/vue/index.js`.\n   202→    *   Create a new file at `assets/vue/index.ts` with the following content:\n   203→\n   204→    ```typescript\n   205→    // polyfill recommended by Vite https://vitejs.dev/config/build-options#build-modulepreload\n   206→    import \"vite/modulepreload-polyfill\"\n   207→    import { Component, h } from \"vue\"\n   208→    import { createLiveVue, findComponent, type LiveHook, type ComponentMap } from \"live_vue\"\n   209→\n   210→    // needed to make $live available in the Vue component\n   211→    declare module \"vue\" {\n   212→      interface ComponentCustomProperties {\n   213→        $live: LiveHook\n   214→      }\n   215→    }\n   216→\n   217→    export default createLiveVue({\n   218→      // name will be passed as-is in v-component of the .vue HEEX component\n   219→      resolve: name => {\n   220→        // we're importing from ../../lib to allow collocating Vue files with LiveView files\n   221→        // eager: true disables lazy loading - all these components will be part of the app.js bundle\n   222→        // more: https://vite.dev/guide/features.html#glob-import\n   223→        const components = {\n   224→          ...import.meta.glob(\"./**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n   225→          ...import.meta.glob(\"../../lib/**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n   226→        } as ComponentMap\n   227→\n   228→        // finds component by name or path suffix and gives a nice error message.\n   229→        // `path/to/component/index.vue` can be found as `path/to/component` or simply `component`\n   230→        // `path/to/Component.vue` can be found as `path/to/Component` or simply `Component`\n   231→        return findComponent(components as ComponentMap, name)\n   232→      },\n   233→      // it's a default implementation of creating and mounting vue app, you can easily extend it to add your own plugins, directives etc.\n   234→      setup: ({ createApp, component, props, slots, plugin, el }) => {\n   235→        const app = createApp({ render: () => h(component as Component, props, slots) })\n   236→        app.use(plugin)\n   237→        // add your own plugins here\n   238→        // app.use(pinia)\n   239→        app.mount(el)\n   240→        return app\n   241→      },\n   242→    })\n   243→    ```\n   244→\n   245→2.  **Update `tsconfig.json`**:\n   246→    Add `vue/index.ts` to the `include` array in your `assets/tsconfig.json` file. The final result should look similar to this:\n   247→\n   248→    ```json\n   249→    {\n   250→      \"compilerOptions\": {\n   251→        // ...\n   252→      },\n   253→      \"include\": [\"js/**/*.ts\", \"js/**/*.js\", \"js/**/*.tsx\", \"vue/**/*.vue\", \"vue/index.ts\"]\n   254→    }\n   255→    ```\n   256→\n   257→### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n   258→\n   259→*   **SSR Attribute Rendering**: Fixed a bug where the `data-ssr` attribute was not being rendered correctly as a boolean `true` or `false` in the final HTML.\n   260→\n   261→### Housekeeping\n   262→\n   263→*   **Optional Floki Dependency**: `floki` is now an optional dependency, only required if you use the new testing utilities.\n   264→*   **Dependency Updates**: NPM dependencies have been updated to address security vulnerabilities.\n   265→*   **Dropped Elixir 1.12 Support**: Support for Elixir 1.12 has been removed to align with Phoenix LiveView's supported versions.\n   266→\n   267→\n   268→## 0.5.7 - 2024-12-04\n   269→\n   270→### Fixes\n   271→\n   272→- Fix the `useLiveVue` hook typings to show all available functions and properties.\n   273→\n   274→\n   275→## 0.5.6 - 2024-11-27\n   276→\n   277→### Improvements\n   278→\n   279→- Much better typing for the library [#41](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/41). Big thanks to [@francois-codes](https://github.com/francois-codes) for the contribution!\n   280→- Added `worker` option to `vite.config.js`, and added instruction how to deal with typescript error [#45](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/45)\n   281→\n   282→\n   283→## 0.5.5 - 2024-11-14\n   284→\n   285→### Fixes\n   286→\n   287→- Slots are now rendered correctly in SSR [#39](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/39)\n   288→\n   289→\n   290→## 0.5.4 - 2024-11-13\n   291→\n   292→### Fixed\n   293→\n   294→- added type: module to package.json in live_vue to fix the older nodejs module resolution issue [#36](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/issues/36)\n   295→\n   296→\n   297→## 0.5.3 - 2024-11-12\n   298→\n   299→### Fixed\n   300→\n   301→- Added explicit extensions to all JS imports. It should fix some issues with module resulution. [#36](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/issues/36)\n   302→\n   303→\n   304→## 0.5.2 - 2024-10-08\n   305→\n   306→### Changed\n   307→\n   308→- Added hint to pass `--silent` flag to `npm` watcher in `INSTALLATION.md`. It prevents `npm` from printing executed command which is not useful and makes output messy.\n   309→\n   310→```elixir\n   311→config :my_app, MyAppWeb.Endpoint,\n   312→  # ...\n   313→  watchers: [\n   314→    npm: [\"--silent\", \"run\", \"dev\", cd: Path.expand(\"../assets\", __DIR__)]\n   315→  ]\n   316→```\n   317→\n   318→\n   319→## 0.5.1 - 2024-10-08\n   320→\n   321→### Fixed\n   322→\n   323→- Fixed a bug where the server was not preloading the correct assets for the Vue components. It happened because CursorAI \"skipped\" important part of the code when migrating to the TypeScript 😅\n   324→\n   325→\n   326→## 0.5.0 - 2024-10-08\n   327→\n   328→### Changed\n   329→\n   330→- Migrated the project to TypeScript 💜 [#32](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/32)\n   331→- Added `createLiveVue` entrypoint to make it easier to customize Vue app initialization\n   332→\n   333→\n   334→### Deprecations\n   335→\n   336→- `assets/vue/index.js` should export app created by `createLiveVue()`, not just available components. See migration below.\n   337→\n   338→\n   339→### Migration\n   340→\n   341→In `assets/js/app.js`, instead of:\n   342→\n   343→```js\n   344→export default {\n   345→  ...import.meta.glob(\"./**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n   346→  ...import.meta.glob(\"../../lib/**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n   347→}\n   348→```\n   349→\n   350→use:\n   351→```js\n   352→// polyfill recommended by Vite https://vitejs.dev/config/build-options#build-modulepreload\n   353→import \"vite/modulepreload-polyfill\"\n   354→import { h } from \"vue\"\n   355→import { createLiveVue, findComponent } from \"live_vue\"\n   356→\n   357→export default createLiveVue({\n   358→  resolve: name => {\n   359→    const components = {\n   360→      ...import.meta.glob(\"./**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n   361→      ...import.meta.glob(\"../../lib/**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n   362→    }\n   363→\n   364→    // finds component by name or path suffix and gives a nice error message.\n   365→    // `path/to/component/index.vue` can be found as `path/to/component` or simply `component`\n   366→    // `path/to/Component.vue` can be found as `path/to/Component` or simply `Component`\n   367→    return findComponent(components, name)\n   368→  },\n   369→  setup: ({ createApp, component, props, slots, plugin, el }) => {\n   370→    const app = createApp({ render: () => h(component, props, slots) })\n   371→    app.use(plugin)\n   372→    app.mount(el)\n   373→    return app\n   374→  },\n   375→})\n   376→```\n   377→\n   378→then, in `assets/js/app.js`, instead of:\n   379→\n   380→```js\n   381→import components from \"./vue\"\n   382→```\n   383→\n   384→simply do\n   385→\n   386→```js\n   387→import { getHooks } from \"live_vue\"\n   388→import liveVueApp from \"./vue\"\n   389→// ...\n   390→\n   391→const hooks = { ...getHooks(liveVueApp) }\n   392→```\n   393→\n   394→If you had any custom initialization code, you have to move it to `createLiveVue().setup()` function.\n   395→\n   396→\n   397→### Fixed\n   398→\n   399→- Nicely formatted JS error stracktraces during SSR [commit](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/commit/10f672bce4104a38523905c52c4879083e4bc6db)\n   400→- Previously `initializeVueApp` was not working in SSR mode, since it was declared in app.js which couldn't be imported by server bundle. Now it's in a separate file as `createLiveVue().setup()` and can be imported by both client and server bundles.\n   401→\n   402→\n   403→## 0.4.1 - 2024-08-30\n   404→\n   405→### Changed\n   406→\n   407→-   Improved `pathToFullPathAndFilename` to work with `index.vue` files. Now `../ComponentName/index.vue` can be referenced as `ComponentName` [#23](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/23)\n   408→\n   409→\n   410→## 0.4.0 - 2024-06-12\n   411→\n   412→### New feature\n   413→\n   414→-   Support for custom Vue instance initialization [#13](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/13) by @morfert\n   415→\n   416→\n   417→## 0.3.9 - 2024-06-07\n   418→\n   419→\n   420→\n   421→\n   422→## 0.3.8 - 2024-06-01\n   423→\n   424→### Fixed\n   425→\n   426→-   Invalid live_vue import in copied package.json (`file:../..` -> `file:../deps/live_vue`)\n   427→-   Changed `useLiveVue` inject key from `Symbol()` to `_live_vue` string, so it's working if Vite does a reload and Symbol is re-evaluated.\n   428→\n   429→### Added\n   430→\n   431→-   Added live_vue, phoenix, phoenix_html and phonenix_live_vue to vite `optimizeDeps.include` config options. It should pre-bundle these packages in development, making it consistent with packages imported from node_modules and improve DX.\n   432→-   Added initial typescript definitions. Apparently it's enough to name them `<filename>.d.mts`, so I've created them both for `index.mjs` and `server.mjs`\n   433→\n   434→\n   435→## 0.3.7 - 2024-05-26\n   436→\n   437→### Changed\n   438→\n   439→-   Added a Mix.Task to make JS file setup more straightforward and cross-platform [#11](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/11). Contribution by @morfert 🔥\n   440→-   Installation instruction was moved to the separate file\n   441→-   Package.json was added to files automatically copied from live_vue when using `mix live_vue.setup`\n   442→\n   443→### Fixed\n   444→\n   445→-   Removed `build: {modulePreload: { polyfill: false }}` from vite.config.js as it made it impossible to use `vite/modulepreload-polyfill`. To migrate: please remove that line from yours vite.config.js. Fixed [#12](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/issues/12)\n   446→\n   447→\n   448→## 0.3.6 - 2024-05-24\n   449→\n   450→### Fixed\n   451→\n   452→-   Fixed missing import in loadManifest\n   453→-   Added `import \"vite/modulepreload-polyfill\";` to `assets/vue/index.js`. To migrate, add that line to the top. It adds polyfill for module preload, required for some browsers. More here: https://vitejs.dev/config/build-options#build-modulepreload\n   454→\n   455→\n   456→## 0.3.5 - 2024-05-24\n   457→\n   458→### Changed\n   459→\n   460→-   Removed `body-parser` dependency from `live_vue`. Should fix [#9](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/issues/9)\n   461→\n   462→\n   463→## 0.3.4 - 2024-05-22\n   464→\n   465→### Fixed\n   466→\n   467→-   Props are correctly updated when being arrays of structs\n   468→\n   469→\n   470→## 0.3.3 - 2024-05-22\n   471→\n   472→### Fixed\n   473→\n   474→-   Javascript imports were mixed - vitePlugin.js was using CJS, rest was using ESM. Now it's explicit by adding \".mjs\" extension.\n   475→-   Removed `:attr` declarations for `<.vue>` component to avoid warnings related to unexpected props being passed to `:rest` attribute [#8](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/pull/8)\n   476→\n   477→\n   478→## 0.3.2 - 2024-05-19\n   479→\n   480→### Fixed\n   481→\n   482→-   Hot reload of CSS when updating Elixir files\n   483→\n   484→## 0.3.1 - 2024-05-17\n   485→\n   486→### Changed\n   487→\n   488→-   Simplified `assets/vue/index.js` file - mapping filenames to keys is done by the library. Previous version should still work.\n   489→\n   490→## 0.3.0 - 2024-05-17\n   491→\n   492→### CHANGED\n   493→\n   494→-   removed esbuild from live_vue, `package.json` points directly to `assets/js/live_vue`\n   495→-   added support to lazy loading components. See more in README. To migrate, ensure all steps from installation are up-to-date.\n   496→\n   497→## 0.2.0 - 2024-05-17\n   498→\n   499→QoL release\n   500→\n   501→### Added\n   502→\n   503→-   `@` added to Vite & typescript paths. To migrate, see `assets/copy/tsconfig.json` and `assets/copy/vite.config.js`\n   504→-   Added Vite types to tsconfig.json to support special imports, eg. svg. To migrate, add `\"types\": [\"vite/client\"]`.\n   505→-   Added possibility to colocate Vue files in `lib` directory. To migrate, copy `assets/copy/vue/index.js` to your project.\n   506→\n   507→### Changed\n   508→\n   509→-   Adjusted files hierarchy to match module names\n   510→-   Publishing with expublish\n   511→\n   512→## [0.1.0] - 2024-05-15\n   513→\n   514→### Initial release\n   515→\n   516→-   Start of the project\n   517→-   End-To-End Reactivity with LiveView\n   518→-   Server-Side Rendered (SSR) Vue\n   519→-   Tailwind Support\n   520→-   Dead View Support\n   521→-   Vite support\n   522→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013ZQxJcEnb8yScJd143QixN","session_id":"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d","uuid":"754fad4f-0e5d-4f37-9ba1-c4e2352d7a60"}
