{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCTetTL28kFe2RN6S3zBDT","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Component Reference\n     2→\n     3→This guide provides a complete reference for using Vue components in Phoenix LiveView templates.\n     4→\n     5→> #### Practical Examples {: .tip}\n     6→>\n     7→> For practical usage examples and patterns, see [Basic Usage](basic_usage.md). This reference focuses on complete syntax documentation.\n     8→\n     9→## The `.vue` Component\n    10→\n    11→The `.vue` component is the primary way to render Vue components in LiveView templates.\n    12→\n    13→### Basic Syntax\n    14→\n    15→```elixir\n    16→<.vue\n    17→  v-component=\"ComponentName\"\n    18→  v-socket={@socket}\n    19→  prop_name={@value}\n    20→/>\n    21→```\n    22→\n    23→For practical examples of different rendering patterns, see [Basic Usage](basic_usage.md#rendering-components).\n    24→\n    25→### Required Attributes\n    26→\n    27→| Attribute | Type | Description | Example |\n    28→|-----------|------|-------------|---------|\n    29→| `v-component` | `string` | Vue component name or path | `\"Counter\"`, `\"admin/Dashboard\"` |\n    30→| `v-socket` | `Phoenix.LiveView.Socket` | LiveView socket (required in LiveView) | `{@socket}` |\n    31→\n    32→### Optional Attributes\n    33→\n    34→| Attribute | Type | Default | Description |\n    35→|-----------|------|---------|-------------|\n    36→| `id` | `string` | auto-generated | Explicit wrapper element ID |\n    37→| `class` | `string` | `nil` | CSS classes for wrapper element |\n    38→| `v-ssr` | `boolean` | `true` | Enable/disable server-side rendering |\n    39→| `v-diff` | `boolean` | `true` | Enable/disable props diffing for this component |\n    40→\n    41→### Event Handlers\n    42→\n    43→Event handlers use the `v-on:` prefix to handle Vue component events.\n    44→\n    45→| Pattern | Description | Example |\n    46→|---------|-------------|---------|\n    47→| `v-on:event-name` | Handle Vue emit events | `v-on:save={JS.push(\"save\")}` |\n    48→\n    49→### Props\n    50→\n    51→All other attributes are passed as props to the Vue component. They are JSON-encoded - you need to either provide serializable types or implement [Jason.Encoder protocol](https://hexdocs.pm/jason/Jason.Encoder.html) for your custom types.\n    52→\n    53→```elixir\n    54→<.vue\n    55→  v-component=\"UserProfile\"\n    56→  v-socket={@socket}\n    57→  user={@user}\n    58→  settings={@settings}\n    59→  is_admin={@current_user.admin?}\n    60→  count={42}\n    61→  items={@list}\n    62→/>\n    63→```\n    64→\n    65→## Component Shortcuts\n    66→\n    67→When using `LiveVue.Components`, you can use shortcut syntax instead of the full `v-component` attribute.\n    68→\n    69→### Setup\n    70→\n    71→```elixir\n    72→# In lib/my_app_web.ex\n    73→defp html_helpers do\n    74→  quote do\n    75→    use LiveVue.Components, vue_root: [\n    76→      \"./assets/vue\",\n    77→      \"./lib/my_app_web\"\n    78→    ]\n    79→  end\n    80→end\n    81→```\n    82→\n    83→### Usage\n    84→\n    85→```elixir\n    86→# Instead of\n    87→<.vue v-component=\"Counter\" v-socket={@socket} count={@count} />\n    88→\n    89→# You can use\n    90→<.Counter v-socket={@socket} count={@count} />\n    91→```\n    92→\n    93→### Component Resolution\n    94→\n    95→Components are resolved by file name.\n    96→\n    97→| File Path | Component Name | Shortcut |\n    98→|-----------|----------------|----------|\n    99→| `assets/vue/Counter.vue` | `\"Counter\"` | `<.Counter />` |\n   100→| `assets/vue/admin/Dashboard.vue` | `\"Dashboard\"` | `<.Dashboard />` |\n   101→\n   102→For components with identical names, use `.vue` component with unambiguous path:\n   103→```elixir\n   104→<.vue v-component=\"admin/Modal\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   105→<.vue v-component=\"public/Modal\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   106→```\n   107→\n   108→## Slots\n   109→\n   110→Vue components can receive slots from LiveView templates.\n   111→\n   112→### Basic Slots\n   113→\n   114→```elixir\n   115→<.vue v-component=\"Card\" v-socket={@socket}>\n   116→  <p>This content goes to the default slot</p>\n   117→  <.icon name=\"hero-star\" />\n   118→</.vue>\n   119→```\n   120→\n   121→```html\n   122→<!-- Card.vue -->\n   123→<template>\n   124→  <div class=\"card\">\n   125→    <slot></slot>\n   126→  </div>\n   127→</template>\n   128→```\n   129→\n   130→### Named Slots\n   131→\n   132→```elixir\n   133→<.vue v-component=\"Modal\" v-socket={@socket}>\n   134→  <:header>\n   135→    <h2>Modal Title</h2>\n   136→  </:header>\n   137→\n   138→  <p>Modal content goes here</p>\n   139→\n   140→  <:footer>\n   141→    <button>Cancel</button>\n   142→    <button>Save</button>\n   143→  </:footer>\n   144→</.vue>\n   145→```\n   146→\n   147→```html\n   148→<!-- Modal.vue -->\n   149→<template>\n   150→  <div class=\"modal\">\n   151→    <header>\n   152→      <slot name=\"header\"></slot>\n   153→    </header>\n   154→\n   155→    <main>\n   156→      <slot></slot>\n   157→    </main>\n   158→\n   159→    <footer>\n   160→      <slot name=\"footer\"></slot>\n   161→    </footer>\n   162→  </div>\n   163→</template>\n   164→```\n   165→\n   166→### Slot Limitations\n   167→\n   168→- Each slot is wrapped in a `div` element (technical limitation)\n   169→- Slots are rendered server-side, so they can't contain Vue components\n   170→- Phoenix hooks don't work inside slots\n   171→- Slots remain reactive and update when their content changes\n   172→\n   173→## Event Handling\n   174→\n   175→### Phoenix Events (Recommended)\n   176→\n   177→Standard Phoenix events work directly in Vue components:\n   178→\n   179→```elixir\n   180→<.vue v-component=\"Form\" v-socket={@socket}>\n   181→  <!-- These work inside Vue components -->\n   182→  <button phx-click=\"save\">Save</button>\n   183→  <input phx-change=\"validate\" />\n   184→  <form phx-submit=\"submit\">...</form>\n   185→</.vue>\n   186→```\n   187→\n   188→For more event handling patterns and examples, see [Basic Usage](basic_usage.md#handling-events).\n   189→\n   190→### Vue Event Handlers\n   191→\n   192→Use `v-on:` for handling Vue component events:\n   193→\n   194→```elixir\n   195→<.vue\n   196→  v-component=\"Counter\"\n   197→  v-socket={@socket}\n   198→  count={@count}\n   199→  v-on:increment={JS.push(\"inc\")}\n   200→  v-on:decrement={JS.push(\"dec\")}\n   201→  v-on:reset={JS.push(\"reset\")}\n   202→/>\n   203→```\n   204→\n   205→For client-side event handling within Vue components, see [Client-Side API](client_api.md#uselivevue).\n   206→\n   207→### Event Payload Handling\n   208→\n   209→When using `JS.push()` without a value, the emit payload is automatically used:\n   210→\n   211→```html\n   212→<!-- Vue component -->\n   213→<button @click=\"$emit('save', { data: formData })\">Save</button>\n   214→```\n   215→\n   216→```elixir\n   217→<!-- LiveView template -->\n   218→<.vue v-on:save={JS.push(\"save\")} />\n   219→<!-- Equivalent to: JS.push(\"save\", data: formData) -->\n   220→```\n   221→\n   222→### Complex Event Handlers\n   223→\n   224→```elixir\n   225→<.vue\n   226→  v-component=\"DataTable\"\n   227→  v-socket={@socket}\n   228→  v-on:sort={JS.push(\"sort\") |> JS.patch(\"/sorted\")}\n   229→  v-on:filter={JS.push(\"filter\") |> JS.show(to: \"#loading\")}\n   230→  v-on:export={JS.push(\"export\") |> JS.navigate(\"/download\")}\n   231→/>\n   232→```\n   233→\n   234→## Server-Side Rendering (SSR)\n   235→\n   236→### Global SSR Configuration\n   237→\n   238→For complete SSR configuration options, see [Configuration](configuration.md#server-side-rendering-ssr).\n   239→\n   240→### Per-Component SSR Control\n   241→\n   242→```elixir\n   243→<!-- Enable SSR for this component -->\n   244→<.vue v-component=\"HeavyComponent\" v-ssr={true} v-socket={@socket} />\n   245→\n   246→<!-- Disable SSR for this component -->\n   247→<.vue v-component=\"ClientOnlyWidget\" v-ssr={false} v-socket={@socket} />\n   248→\n   249→<!-- Use global default -->\n   250→<.vue v-component=\"RegularComponent\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   251→```\n   252→\n   253→## Props Diffing\n   254→\n   255→LiveVue optimizes performance by sending only prop changes (diffs) instead of complete props on every update. This behavior can be controlled both globally and per-component.\n   256→\n   257→### Global Configuration\n   258→\n   259→For complete diffing configuration, see [Configuration - Testing Configuration](configuration.md#testing-configuration).\n   260→\n   261→```elixir\n   262→# config/config.exs\n   263→config :live_vue,\n   264→  enable_props_diff: true  # Default: true\n   265→```\n   266→\n   267→### Per-Component Diff Control\n   268→\n   269→Override global diffing settings for specific components:\n   270→\n   271→```elixir\n   272→<!-- Enable diffing for this component (default) -->\n   273→<.vue v-component=\"OptimizedComponent\" v-diff={true} v-socket={@socket} />\n   274→\n   275→<!-- Disable diffing - always send full props -->\n   276→<.vue v-component=\"TestComponent\" v-diff={false} v-socket={@socket} />\n   277→\n   278→<!-- Use global default -->\n   279→<.vue v-component=\"RegularComponent\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   280→```\n   281→\n   282→### When to Disable Diffing\n   283→\n   284→Consider disabling diffing for:\n   285→- **Testing scenarios** where you need complete props state inspection\n   286→- **Debugging complex prop updates** to see full component state\n   287→- **Components with simple prop structures** where diffing overhead isn't beneficial\n   288→- **Development troubleshooting** when diffing behavior is suspected of causing issues\n   289→\n   290→### Performance Impact\n   291→\n   292→| Setting | Network Payload | Memory Usage | Update Speed |\n   293→|---------|----------------|--------------|--------------|\n   294→| `v-diff={true}` | Minimal (only changes) | Lower | Faster |\n   295→| `v-diff={false}` | Larger (full props) | Higher | Slightly slower |\n   296→\n   297→### SSR Behavior\n   298→\n   299→| Context | SSR Enabled | Behavior |\n   300→|---------|-------------|----------|\n   301→| Initial page load | Yes | Component rendered on server |\n   302→| Live navigation | No | Client-side rendering only |\n   303→| WebSocket update | No | Client-side rendering only |\n   304→| Dead view | Yes | Server-side rendering |\n   305→\n   306→## Data Types and Serialization\n   307→\n   308→### Supported Prop Types\n   309→\n   310→| Elixir Type | Vue Type | Example |\n   311→|-------------|----------|---------|\n   312→| `string` | `string` | `name={\"John\"}` |\n   313→| `integer` | `number` | `count={42}` |\n   314→| `float` | `number` | `price={19.99}` |\n   315→| `boolean` | `boolean` | `active={true}` |\n   316→| `list` | `array` | `items={[1, 2, 3]}` |\n   317→| `map` | `object` | `user={%{name: \"John\"}}` |\n   318→| `nil` | `null` | `optional={nil}` |\n   319→\n   320→### Phoenix LiveView Upload Types\n   321→\n   322→Phoenix LiveView upload configurations are automatically encoded for use with the [`useLiveUpload()`](client_api.md#useliveuploadevent-callback) composable:\n   323→\n   324→| Elixir Type | Vue Type | Usage |\n   325→|-------------|----------|-------|\n   326→| `%Phoenix.LiveView.UploadConfig{}` | `UploadConfig` | `upload={@uploads.documents}` |\n   327→| `%Phoenix.LiveView.UploadEntry{}` | `UploadEntry` | Automatically included in config |\n   328→\n   329→These types are pre-configured with the `LiveVue.Encoder` protocol and work seamlessly with file upload functionality.\n   330→\n   331→### Custom Structs with LiveVue.Encoder\n   332→\n   333→When passing custom structs as props, you must implement the `LiveVue.Encoder` protocol to ensure they are properly serialized and can be diffed efficiently. This protocol is similar to `Jason.Encoder` but converts structs to maps instead of JSON strings.\n   334→\n   335→#### Deriving the Protocol\n   336→\n   337→The simplest way to implement the protocol is by deriving it:\n   338→\n   339→```elixir\n   340→# Encode all fields except :__struct__\n   341→defmodule User do\n   342→  @derive LiveVue.Encoder\n   343→  defstruct [:name, :email, :age]\n   344→end\n   345→\n   346→# Encode only specific fields\n   347→defmodule User do\n   348→  @derive {LiveVue.Encoder, only: [:name, :email]}\n   349→  defstruct [:name, :email, :password, :admin_notes]\n   350→end\n   351→\n   352→# Encode all fields except sensitive ones\n   353→defmodule User do\n   354→  @derive {LiveVue.Encoder, except: [:password, :secret_key]}\n   355→  defstruct [:name, :email, :password, :secret_key]\n   356→end\n   357→\n   358→# For Ecto schemas with associations that may not be loaded\n   359→defmodule Post do\n   360→  use Ecto.Schema\n   361→  @derive {LiveVue.Encoder, except: [:__meta__], nilify_not_loaded: true}\n   362→\n   363→  schema \"posts\" do\n   364→    field :title, :string\n   365→    belongs_to :author, User  # Will be nil if not preloaded, instead of raising\n   366→  end\n   367→end\n   368→```\n   369→\n   370→The `nilify_not_loaded: true` option converts Ecto's `%Ecto.Association.NotLoaded{}` structs to `nil` instead of raising an error. This is useful when you want to pass Ecto schemas as props without always preloading all associations.\n   371→\n   372→#### Custom Implementation\n   373→\n   374→For more control, implement the protocol manually:\n   375→\n   376→```elixir\n   377→defmodule User do\n   378→  defstruct [:name, :email, :password, :profile]\n   379→end\n   380→\n   381→defimpl LiveVue.Encoder, for: User do\n   382→  def encode(user, opts) do\n   383→    %{\n   384→      name: user.name,\n   385→      email: user.email,\n   386→      # Transform nested data as needed\n   387→      profile: Map.take(user.profile, [:avatar, :bio])\n   388→    }\n   389→    |> LiveVue.Encoder.encode(opts)\n   390→  end\n   391→end\n   392→```\n   393→\n   394→#### For Third-Party Structs\n   395→\n   396→If you don't own the struct, use `Protocol.derive/3`:\n   397→\n   398→```elixir\n   399→# In your application startup or module\n   400→Protocol.derive(LiveVue.Encoder, SomeLibrary.User, only: [:id, :name])\n   401→```\n   402→\n   403→#### Why LiveVue.Encoder is Required\n   404→\n   405→The encoder protocol serves several important purposes:\n   406→\n   407→1. **Security**: Prevents accidental exposure of sensitive fields\n   408→2. **Performance**: Enables efficient JSON patch diffing by converting structs to maps\n   409→3. **Explicit Control**: Forces developers to be intentional about what data is sent to the client\n   410→4. **Optimization**: Allows LiveVue to calculate minimal diffs for prop updates\n   411→\n   412→Without implementing this protocol, you'll get a `Protocol.UndefinedError` when trying to pass custom structs as props.\n   413→\n   414→### Complex Data Structures\n   415→\n   416→```elixir\n   417→<.vue\n   418→  v-component=\"UserDashboard\"\n   419→  v-socket={@socket}\n   420→  user={%{\n   421→    id: 1,\n   422→    name: \"John Doe\",\n   423→    email: \"john@example.com\",\n   424→    preferences: %{\n   425→      theme: \"dark\",\n   426→      notifications: true\n   427→    }\n   428→  }}\n   429→  permissions={[\"read\", \"write\", \"admin\"]}\n   430→  metadata={%{\n   431→    last_login: ~U[2023-01-01 12:00:00Z],\n   432→    login_count: 42\n   433→  }}\n   434→/>\n   435→```\n   436→\n   437→### Date and Time Handling\n   438→\n   439→```elixir\n   440→# Dates are serialized as ISO strings\n   441→<.vue\n   442→  v-component=\"Calendar\"\n   443→  v-socket={@socket}\n   444→  current_date={Date.utc_today()}\n   445→  created_at={DateTime.utc_now()}\n   446→/>\n   447→```\n   448→\n   449→```html\n   450→<!-- Vue component -->\n   451→<script setup>\n   452→const props = defineProps<{\n   453→  current_date: string  // \"2023-12-01\"\n   454→  created_at: string    // \"2023-12-01T12:00:00Z\"\n   455→}>()\n   456→\n   457→// Convert to JavaScript Date objects\n   458→const currentDate = new Date(props.current_date)\n   459→const createdAt = new Date(props.created_at)\n   460→</script>\n   461→```\n   462→\n   463→## Error Handling\n   464→\n   465→### Component Not Found\n   466→\n   467→```elixir\n   468→<!-- This will log an error to the console if Counter.vue doesn't exist -->\n   469→<.vue v-component=\"Counter\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   470→```\n   471→\n   472→### Invalid Props\n   473→\n   474→```elixir\n   475→<!-- Vue will warn in console about type mismatches in development -->\n   476→<.vue\n   477→  v-component=\"UserProfile\"\n   478→  v-socket={@socket}\n   479→  user_id=\"not-a-number\"  <!-- Should be integer -->\n   480→/>\n   481→```\n   482→\n   483→### SSR Errors\n   484→\n   485→```elixir\n   486→<!-- SSR errors are logged but don't break the page -->\n   487→<.vue v-component=\"ProblematicComponent\" v-ssr={true} v-socket={@socket} />\n   488→```\n   489→\n   490→## Performance Considerations\n   491→\n   492→### Prop Optimization\n   493→\n   494→```elixir\n   495→# ✅ Good: Only pass what's needed\n   496→<.vue\n   497→  v-component=\"UserCard\"\n   498→  v-socket={@socket}\n   499→  user={%{name: @user.name, avatar: @user.avatar}}\n   500→/>\n   501→\n   502→# ❌ Avoid: Passing large objects unnecessarily\n   503→<.vue\n   504→  v-component=\"UserCard\"\n   505→  v-socket={@socket}\n   506→  user={@user}  # Contains many unused fields\n   507→/>\n   508→```\n   509→\n   510→## Best Practices\n   511→\n   512→### Component Organization\n   513→\n   514→```elixir\n   515→# ✅ Good: Descriptive component names\n   516→<.vue v-component=\"UserProfileCard\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   517→<.vue v-component=\"admin/UserManagementTable\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   518→\n   519→# ❌ Avoid: Generic names\n   520→<.vue v-component=\"Component\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   521→<.vue v-component=\"Widget\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   522→```\n   523→\n   524→### Prop Naming\n   525→\n   526→```elixir\n   527→# ✅ Good: Clear, descriptive prop names\n   528→<.vue\n   529→  v-component=\"ProductCard\"\n   530→  v-socket={@socket}\n   531→  product_name={@product.name}\n   532→  is_featured={@product.featured?}\n   533→  price_in_cents={@product.price}\n   534→/>\n   535→\n   536→# ❌ Avoid: Ambiguous prop names\n   537→<.vue\n   538→  v-component=\"ProductCard\"\n   539→  v-socket={@socket}\n   540→  name={@product.name}\n   541→  flag={@product.featured?}\n   542→  amount={@product.price}\n   543→/>\n   544→```\n   545→\n   546→### Event Naming\n   547→\n   548→```elixir\n   549→# ✅ Good: Descriptive event names\n   550→<.vue\n   551→  v-component=\"ShoppingCart\"\n   552→  v-socket={@socket}\n   553→  v-on:item-added={JS.push(\"add_item\")}\n   554→  v-on:checkout-started={JS.push(\"start_checkout\")}\n   555→/>\n   556→\n   557→# ❌ Avoid: Generic event names\n   558→<.vue\n   559→  v-component=\"ShoppingCart\"\n   560→  v-socket={@socket}\n   561→  v-on:click={JS.push(\"handle_click\")}\n   562→  v-on:action={JS.push(\"do_action\")}\n   563→/>\n   564→```\n   565→\n   566→## Common Patterns\n   567→\n   568→### Data Display Components\n   569→\n   570→```elixir\n   571→<.vue\n   572→  v-component=\"DataTable\"\n   573→  v-socket={@socket}\n   574→  items={@users}\n   575→  columns={[\"name\", \"email\", \"created_at\"]}\n   576→  sortable={true}\n   577→  v-on:sort={JS.push(\"sort_users\")}\n   578→  v-on:filter={JS.push(\"filter_users\")}\n   579→/>\n   580→```\n   581→\n   582→## Troubleshooting\n   583→\n   584→### Component Not Rendering\n   585→\n   586→1. Check component name spelling and case sensitivity\n   587→2. Verify `v-socket={@socket}` is present in LiveView\n   588→3. Ensure component file exists in configured paths\n   589→4. Check browser console for JavaScript errors\n   590→\n   591→### Props Not Updating\n   592→\n   593→1. Verify prop names match between LiveView and Vue\n   594→2. Check that LiveView assigns are actually changing\n   595→3. Ensure `@socket` is connected (not in dead view)\n   596→\n   597→### Events Not Working\n   598→\n   599→1. Check event name spelling in both Vue emit and LiveView handler\n   600→2. Verify `handle_event/3` function exists in LiveView\n   601→3. Check event payload structure matches expectations\n   602→\n   603→## Next Steps\n   604→\n   605→- [Basic Usage](basic_usage.md) for practical patterns and examples\n   606→- [Client-Side API](client_api.md) for Vue component development\n   607→- [Configuration](configuration.md) for advanced setup and customization\n   608→- [Testing](testing.md) for testing component integration\n   609→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R45EXfaLjZgcqByia7QETz","session_id":"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d","uuid":"d1699bb3-b9d2-4ec1-9f96-e498071fb618"}
