{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S7eepQcicdHzaY98BqKd47","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Troubleshooting Guide\n     2→\n     3→This guide helps you diagnose and fix common issues when working with LiveVue.\n     4→\n     5→> #### Quick Start {: .tip}\n     6→>\n     7→> New to LiveVue? Start with [Getting Started](getting_started.md) for a working example, then check [Basic Usage](basic_usage.md) for common patterns.\n     8→\n     9→## Component Issues\n    10→\n    11→### Component Not Rendering\n    12→\n    13→**Symptoms:**\n    14→- Empty div where component should be\n    15→- No errors in console\n    16→- Component works in isolation\n    17→\n    18→**Possible Causes & Solutions:**\n    19→\n    20→1. **Missing `v-socket` attribute**\n    21→   ```elixir\n    22→   # ❌ Missing v-socket\n    23→   <.vue v-component=\"Counter\" count={@count} />\n    24→\n    25→   # ✅ Correct\n    26→   <.vue v-component=\"Counter\" count={@count} v-socket={@socket} />\n    27→   ```\n    28→\n    29→2. **Component name mismatch**\n    30→   ```elixir\n    31→   # ❌ File: Counter.vue, but using wrong name\n    32→   <.vue v-component=\"counter\" v-socket={@socket} />\n    33→\n    34→   # ✅ Correct - case sensitive\n    35→   <.vue v-component=\"Counter\" v-socket={@socket} />\n    36→   ```\n    37→\n    38→   Check browser console for errors.\n    39→\n    40→3. **Component not found in resolution**\n    41→   ```javascript\n    42→   // Check your component resolution in assets/vue/index.js\n    43→   const components = {\n    44→     ...import.meta.glob(\"./**/*.vue\", { eager: true }),\n    45→   }\n    46→\n    47→   // Debug: log available components\n    48→   console.log(\"Available components:\", Object.keys(components))\n    49→   ```\n    50→\n    51→### Component Renders But Doesn't Update\n    52→\n    53→**Symptoms:**\n    54→- Component shows initial state\n    55→- Props don't update when server state changes\n    56→- No reactivity\n    57→\n    58→**Solutions:**\n    59→\n    60→1. **Check prop names match**\n    61→   ```elixir\n    62→   # Server side\n    63→   <.vue user_name={@user.name} v-component=\"Profile\" v-socket={@socket} />\n    64→   ```\n    65→\n    66→   ```html\n    67→   <!-- Client side - prop names must match exactly -->\n    68→   <script setup>\n    69→   const props = defineProps<{\n    70→     user_name: string  // Must match server prop name\n    71→   }>()\n    72→   </script>\n    73→   ```\n    74→\n    75→2. **Verify assigns are updating**\n    76→   ```elixir\n    77→   # Add debug logging\n    78→   def handle_event(\"update\", _params, socket) do\n    79→     IO.inspect(socket.assigns, label: \"Before update\")\n    80→     socket = assign(socket, :count, socket.assigns.count + 1)\n    81→     IO.inspect(socket.assigns, label: \"After update\")\n    82→     {:noreply, socket}\n    83→   end\n    84→   ```\n    85→\n    86→3. **Use Vue.js devtools to inspect the component**\n    87→\n    88→   Open Vue.js devtools in browser and inspect the component.\n    89→   Check if the component is receiving the correct props.\n    90→   Check if the component is re-rendering when the props change.\n    91→\n    92→### LiveVue.Encoder Protocol Issues\n    93→\n    94→**Symptoms:**\n    95→- `Protocol.UndefinedError` when passing structs as props\n    96→- Component doesn't render with custom struct props\n    97→- Error mentions \"LiveVue.Encoder protocol must always be explicitly implemented\"\n    98→\n    99→**Solutions:**\n   100→\n   101→1. **Implement the encoder protocol for your structs**\n   102→   ```elixir\n   103→   defmodule User do\n   104→     @derive LiveVue.Encoder\n   105→     defstruct [:name, :email, :age]\n   106→   end\n   107→   ```\n   108→\n   109→2. **For third-party structs, use Protocol.derive/3**\n   110→   ```elixir\n   111→   # In your application.ex or relevant module\n   112→   Protocol.derive(LiveVue.Encoder, SomeLibrary.User, only: [:id, :name])\n   113→   ```\n   114→\n   115→3. **Debug encoder issues**\n   116→   ```elixir\n   117→   # Test your encoder implementation\n   118→   iex> user = %User{name: \"John\", email: \"john@example.com\"}\n   119→   iex> LiveVue.Encoder.encode(user)\n   120→   %{name: \"John\", email: \"john@example.com\"}\n   121→   ```\n   122→\n   123→For complete implementation details including field selection and custom implementations, see [Component Reference](component_reference.md#custom-structs-with-livevue-encoder).\n   124→\n   125→**Common Causes:**\n   126→- Passing structs without implementing the encoder protocol\n   127→- Nested structs where some don't have the protocol implemented\n   128→- Third-party library structs that need protocol derivation\n   129→\n   130→### TypeScript Errors\n   131→\n   132→**Common Error: `Cannot find module 'live_vue'`**\n   133→\n   134→```typescript\n   135→// Add to your env.d.ts or types.d.ts\n   136→declare module 'live_vue' {\n   137→  export function useLiveVue(): any\n   138→  export function createLiveVue(config: any): any\n   139→  export function findComponent(components: any, name: string): any\n   140→  export function getHooks(app: any): any\n   141→}\n   142→```\n   143→\n   144→**Error: `Property 'xxx' does not exist on type`**\n   145→\n   146→```typescript\n   147→// Define proper interfaces\n   148→interface Props {\n   149→  count: number\n   150→  user: {\n   151→    id: number\n   152→    name: string\n   153→  }\n   154→}\n   155→\n   156→const props = defineProps<Props>()\n   157→```\n   158→\n   159→## Event Handling Issues\n   160→\n   161→### Events Not Firing\n   162→\n   163→**Symptoms:**\n   164→- Clicking buttons does nothing\n   165→- No events reach LiveView\n   166→- Console shows no errors\n   167→\n   168→**Solutions:**\n   169→\n   170→1. **Check event handler syntax**\n   171→   ```elixir\n   172→   # ❌ Wrong syntax\n   173→   <.vue v-on-click={JS.push(\"increment\")} />\n   174→\n   175→   # ✅ Correct syntax\n   176→   <.vue v-on:click={JS.push(\"increment\")} />\n   177→   ```\n   178→\n   179→2. **Verify event names match**\n   180→   ```html\n   181→   <!-- Vue component -->\n   182→   <button @click=\"$emit('increment', {amount: 1})\">+1</button>\n   183→   ```\n   184→\n   185→   ```elixir\n   186→   <!-- LiveView template -->\n   187→   <.vue v-on:increment={JS.push(\"inc\")} />\n   188→\n   189→   def handle_event(\"inc\", %{\"amount\" => amount}, socket) do\n   190→     # Handle event\n   191→   end\n   192→   ```\n   193→\n   194→3. **Check payload structure**\n   195→   ```elixir\n   196→   # Debug event payload\n   197→   def handle_event(\"save\", params, socket) do\n   198→     IO.inspect(params, label: \"Event params\")\n   199→     {:noreply, socket}\n   200→   end\n   201→   ```\n   202→\n   203→### Events Fire But Handler Not Called\n   204→\n   205→**Check handler function exists:**\n   206→```elixir\n   207→# Make sure you have the handler defined\n   208→def handle_event(\"my_event\", _params, socket) do\n   209→  {:noreply, socket}\n   210→end\n   211→```\n   212→\n   213→**Verify event name spelling:**\n   214→```elixir\n   215→# Event names are case-sensitive\n   216→<.vue v-on:save-user={JS.push(\"save_user\")} />  # save-user → save_user\n   217→```\n   218→\n   219→## Build and Development Issues\n   220→\n   221→### Vite Server Not Starting\n   222→\n   223→**Error: `EADDRINUSE: address already in use`**\n   224→\n   225→```bash\n   226→# Kill process using port 5173\n   227→lsof -ti:5173 | xargs kill -9\n   228→\n   229→# Or use different port\n   230→npm run dev -- --port 5174\n   231→```\n   232→\n   233→**Error: `Module not found`**\n   234→\n   235→```bash\n   236→# Clear node_modules and reinstall\n   237→rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json\n   238→npm install\n   239→```\n   240→\n   241→### Build Failures\n   242→\n   243→**TypeScript compilation errors:**\n   244→\n   245→```bash\n   246→# Check TypeScript version compatibility\n   247→npm install typescript@5.5.4 vue-tsc@2.10.0\n   248→```\n   249→\n   250→**Vite build errors:**\n   251→\n   252→```bash\n   253→# Clear Vite cache\n   254→rm -rf node_modules/.vite\n   255→npm run build\n   256→```\n   257→\n   258→### Hot Reload Not Working\n   259→\n   260→1. **Check Vite configuration:**\n   261→   ```javascript\n   262→   // vite.config.js\n   263→   export default defineConfig({\n   264→     server: {\n   265→       host: '0.0.0.0',  // Allow external connections\n   266→       port: 5173,\n   267→       hmr: true\n   268→     }\n   269→   })\n   270→   ```\n   271→\n   272→2. **Verify watcher configuration:**\n   273→   ```elixir\n   274→   # config/dev.exs\n   275→   config :my_app, MyAppWeb.Endpoint,\n   276→     watchers: [\n   277→       npm: [\"--silent\", \"run\", \"dev\", cd: Path.expand(\"../assets\", __DIR__)]\n   278→     ]\n   279→   ```\n   280→\n   281→3. **Understand HMR scope:**\n   282→   - **Vue files**: Hot Module Replacement works seamlessly - changes to `.vue` files are reflected instantly without page refresh\n   283→   - **Elixir files**: Changes to `.ex` and `.heex` files trigger a LiveView re-render via Phoenix's code reloading, not Vite HMR. This still provides fast feedback but works through LiveView's WebSocket connection rather than Vite's HMR\n   284→\n   285→## SSR Issues\n   286→\n   287→### SSR Not Working\n   288→\n   289→**Check SSR configuration:**\n   290→```elixir\n   291→# config/dev.exs\n   292→config :live_vue,\n   293→  ssr_module: LiveVue.SSR.ViteJS,\n   294→  vite_host: \"http://localhost:5173\",\n   295→  ssr: true\n   296→```\n   297→\n   298→For complete SSR configuration options, see [Configuration](configuration.md#server-side-rendering-ssr).\n   299→\n   300→**Verify Node.js version:**\n   301→```bash\n   302→node --version  # Should be 19+\n   303→```\n   304→\n   305→### SSR Errors in Production\n   306→\n   307→**Check NodeJS supervisor:**\n   308→```elixir\n   309→# application.ex\n   310→children = [\n   311→  {NodeJS.Supervisor, [path: LiveVue.SSR.NodeJS.server_path(), pool_size: 4]},\n   312→  # ... other children\n   313→]\n   314→```\n   315→\n   316→**Verify server bundle exists:**\n   317→```bash\n   318→ls priv/static/server.mjs  # Should exist after build\n   319→```\n   320→\n   321→For production SSR setup details, see [Configuration](configuration.md#production-ssr-setup).\n   322→\n   323→## Performance Issues\n   324→\n   325→### Slow Initial Load\n   326→\n   327→1. **Enable lazy loading:**\n   328→   ```javascript\n   329→   // assets/vue/index.js\n   330→   const components = {\n   331→     Counter: () => import('./Counter.vue'),\n   332→     Modal: () => import('./Modal.vue')\n   333→   }\n   334→   ```\n   335→\n   336→2. **Optimize bundle size:**\n   337→   ```bash\n   338→   # Analyze bundle\n   339→   npm run build -- --analyze\n   340→   ```\n   341→\n   342→### Memory Leaks\n   343→\n   344→**Clean up event listeners:**\n   345→```html\n   346→<script setup>\n   347→import { onUnmounted } from 'vue'\n   348→import { useLiveVue } from 'live_vue'\n   349→\n   350→const live = useLiveVue()\n   351→\n   352→const cleanup = live.handleEvent('data_update', handleUpdate)\n   353→\n   354→onUnmounted(() => {\n   355→  cleanup()  // Important: clean up listeners\n   356→})\n   357→</script>\n   358→```\n   359→\n   360→**Clear timers and intervals:**\n   361→```html\n   362→<script setup>\n   363→import { onUnmounted } from 'vue'\n   364→\n   365→const interval = setInterval(() => {\n   366→  // Do something\n   367→}, 1000)\n   368→\n   369→onUnmounted(() => {\n   370→  clearInterval(interval)\n   371→})\n   372→</script>\n   373→```\n   374→\n   375→## Debugging Techniques\n   376→\n   377→### Enable Debug Mode\n   378→\n   379→```javascript\n   380→// In browser console or app.js\n   381→window.liveVueDebug = true\n   382→```\n   383→\n   384→### Component Inspection\n   385→\n   386→1. **Use Vue DevTools browser extension**\n   387→2. **Add debug logging:**\n   388→   ```html\n   389→   <script setup>\n   390→   import { watch } from 'vue'\n   391→\n   392→   const props = defineProps<{count: number}>()\n   393→\n   394→   watch(() => props.count, (newVal, oldVal) => {\n   395→     console.log('Count changed:', oldVal, '→', newVal)\n   396→   })\n   397→   </script>\n   398→   ```\n   399→\n   400→### Network Debugging\n   401→\n   402→1. **Monitor WebSocket traffic in browser DevTools**\n   403→2. **Log LiveView events:**\n   404→   ```elixir\n   405→   def handle_event(event, params, socket) do\n   406→     IO.inspect({event, params}, label: \"LiveView Event\")\n   407→     # ... handle event\n   408→   end\n   409→   ```\n   410→\n   411→## Common Error Messages\n   412→\n   413→### `Cannot read property 'mount' of undefined`\n   414→\n   415→**Cause:** Component resolution failed\n   416→\n   417→**Solution:** Check component name and file path\n   418→```javascript\n   419→// Debug component resolution\n   420→// find component does it by default, you might need to do it if you override it\n   421→console.log(\"Resolving component:\", componentName)\n   422→console.log(\"Available components:\", Object.keys(components))\n   423→```\n   424→\n   425→### `ReferenceError: process is not defined`\n   426→\n   427→**Cause:** Node.js globals in browser code\n   428→\n   429→**Solution:** Add to Vite config:\n   430→```javascript\n   431→// vite.config.js\n   432→export default defineConfig({\n   433→  define: {\n   434→    global: 'globalThis',\n   435→    'process.env': {}\n   436→  }\n   437→})\n   438→```\n   439→\n   440→### `Module \"live_vue\" has been externalized`\n   441→\n   442→**Cause:** SSR configuration issue\n   443→\n   444→**Solution:** Check Vite SSR config:\n   445→```javascript\n   446→// vite.config.js\n   447→export default defineConfig({\n   448→  ssr: {\n   449→    noExternal: ['live_vue']\n   450→  }\n   451→})\n   452→```\n   453→\n   454→## Getting Help\n   455→\n   456→### Before Asking for Help\n   457→\n   458→1. **Check browser console for errors**\n   459→2. **Verify all configuration steps** (see [Configuration](configuration.md))\n   460→3. **Test with minimal reproduction case**\n   461→4. **Create a fresh project with Igniter to verify the issue isn't in your configuration**\n   462→\n   463→### Where to Get Help\n   464→\n   465→1. **GitHub Issues**: For bugs and feature requests\n   466→2. **GitHub Discussions**: For questions and community help\n   467→3. **Elixir Forum**: For general Phoenix/Elixir questions\n   468→4. **Vue.js Discord**: For Vue-specific questions\n   469→\n   470→### Creating Bug Reports\n   471→\n   472→Include:\n   473→1. **LiveVue version**\n   474→2. **Phoenix/LiveView versions**\n   475→3. **Node.js version**\n   476→4. **Minimal reproduction case**\n   477→5. **Error messages and stack traces**\n   478→6. **Browser and OS information**\n   479→\n   480→## Next Steps\n   481→\n   482→- [Live Examples](https://livevue.skalecki.dev) - Working examples to compare against\n   483→- [FAQ](faq.md) for conceptual questions\n   484→- [Architecture](architecture.md) to understand how things work\n   485→- [Configuration](configuration.md) for advanced setup options\n   486→- [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/Valian/live_vue/issues) to report bugs\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R45EXfaLjZgcqByia7QETz","session_id":"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d","uuid":"95ade3a3-9749-49bf-b67a-94f0605f4863"}
