{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XK7ztQCBGyHcwAKijoZXfz","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Forms and Validation\n     2→\n     3→This guide covers the `useLiveForm` composable for building complex forms with server-side validation, nested objects, and dynamic arrays in LiveVue.\n     4→\n     5→> #### Getting Started {: .tip}\n     6→>\n     7→> New to LiveVue? Check out [Basic Usage](basic_usage.md) for fundamental patterns before diving into forms.\n     8→\n     9→## Quick Example\n    10→\n    11→Here's how a typical form setup looks with `useLiveForm`:\n    12→\n    13→**Vue Component:**\n    14→```html\n    15→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n    16→import { useLiveForm, type Form } from 'live_vue'\n    17→\n    18→type UserForm = {\n    19→  name: string\n    20→  email: string\n    21→  profile: {\n    22→    bio: string\n    23→    skills: string[]\n    24→  }\n    25→}\n    26→\n    27→const props = defineProps<{ form: Form<UserForm> }>()\n    28→\n    29→const form = useLiveForm(() => props.form, {\n    30→  changeEvent: 'validate',     // Send validation requests on changes\n    31→  submitEvent: 'submit',       // Event sent on form submission\n    32→  debounceInMiliseconds: 300   // Debounce validation requests\n    33→})\n    34→\n    35→// Access fields with full type safety\n    36→const nameField = form.field('name')\n    37→const emailField = form.field('email')\n    38→const bioField = form.field('profile.bio')\n    39→const skillsArray = form.fieldArray('profile.skills')\n    40→</script>\n    41→\n    42→<template>\n    43→  <div>\n    44→    <!-- Basic field with validation -->\n    45→    <input\n    46→      v-bind=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value\"\n    47→      :class=\"{ error: nameField.isTouched.value && nameField.errorMessage.value }\"\n    48→    />\n    49→    <div v-if=\"nameField.errorMessage.value\">\n    50→      {{ nameField.errorMessage.value }}\n    51→    </div>\n    52→\n    53→    <!-- Array field with add/remove -->\n    54→    <div v-for=\"(skillField, index) in skillsArray.fields.value\" :key=\"index\">\n    55→      <input v-bind=\"skillField.inputAttrs.value\" placeholder=\"Enter skill\" />\n    56→      <button @click=\"skillsArray.remove(index)\">Remove</button>\n    57→    </div>\n    58→    <button @click=\"skillsArray.add('')\">Add Skill</button>\n    59→\n    60→    <!-- Form actions -->\n    61→    <button @click=\"form.submit()\" :disabled=\"!form.isValid.value || form.isValidating.value\">\n    62→      {{ form.isValidating.value ? 'Validating...' : 'Submit' }}\n    63→    </button>\n    64→    <button @click=\"form.reset()\">Reset</button>\n    65→  </div>\n    66→</template>\n    67→```\n    68→\n    69→**LiveView Setup:**\n    70→```elixir\n    71→defmodule MyAppWeb.UserFormLive do\n    72→  use MyAppWeb, :live_view\n    73→\n    74→  def render(assigns) do\n    75→    ~H\"\"\"\n    76→    <.vue form={@form} v-component=\"UserForm\" v-socket={@socket} />\n    77→    \"\"\"\n    78→  end\n    79→\n    80→  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    81→    changeset = User.changeset(%User{}, %{})\n    82→    {:ok, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\n    83→  end\n    84→\n    85→  def handle_event(\"validate\", %{\"user\" => params}, socket) do\n    86→    changeset = User.changeset(%User{}, params)\n    87→    {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\n    88→  end\n    89→\n    90→  def handle_event(\"submit\", %{\"user\" => params}, socket) do\n    91→    changeset = User.changeset(%User{}, params)\n    92→    case Repo.insert(changeset) do\n    93→      {:ok, _user} -> {:noreply, redirect(socket, to: \"/\")}\n    94→      {:error, changeset} -> {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\n    95→    end\n    96→  end\n    97→end\n    98→```\n    99→\n   100→## Why useLiveForm?\n   101→\n   102→Traditional client-side forms present several challenges:\n   103→- **Validation synchronization** between client and server\n   104→- **Complex state management** for nested objects and arrays\n   105→- **Type safety** for deeply nested form structures\n   106→- **Accessibility** and proper ARIA attributes\n   107→- **User experience** patterns like field states and error handling\n   108→\n   109→The `useLiveForm` composable solves these problems by:\n   110→- Providing seamless server-side validation with debouncing\n   111→- Offering type-safe field access for complex structures\n   112→- Managing all form state reactively (dirty, touched, valid)\n   113→- Automatically generating proper input attributes and accessibility features\n   114→- Handling nested objects and dynamic arrays with ease\n   115→\n   116→## Basic Usage\n   117→\n   118→### Setting Up a Form\n   119→\n   120→First, set up your LiveView with form handling:\n   121→\n   122→```elixir\n   123→defmodule MyAppWeb.ContactFormLive do\n   124→  use MyAppWeb, :live_view\n   125→\n   126→  def render(assigns) do\n   127→    ~H\"\"\"\n   128→    <.vue form={@form} v-component=\"ContactForm\" v-socket={@socket} />\n   129→    \"\"\"\n   130→  end\n   131→\n   132→  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n   133→    changeset = Contact.changeset(%Contact{}, %{})\n   134→    {:ok, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :contact))}\n   135→  end\n   136→\n   137→  def handle_event(\"validate\", %{\"contact\" => params}, socket) do\n   138→    changeset = Contact.changeset(%Contact{}, params)\n   139→    {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :contact))}\n   140→  end\n   141→\n   142→  def handle_event(\"submit\", %{\"contact\" => params}, socket) do\n   143→    changeset = Contact.changeset(%Contact{}, params)\n   144→\n   145→    case Repo.insert(changeset) do\n   146→      {:ok, contact} ->\n   147→        {:noreply, put_flash(socket, :info, \"Contact created successfully!\")}\n   148→      {:error, changeset} ->\n   149→        {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :contact))}\n   150→    end\n   151→  end\n   152→end\n   153→```\n   154→\n   155→### Creating the Vue Component\n   156→\n   157→Create a Vue component that uses `useLiveForm`:\n   158→\n   159→```html\n   160→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n   161→import { useLiveForm, type Form } from 'live_vue'\n   162→\n   163→type ContactForm = {\n   164→  name: string\n   165→  email: string\n   166→  subject: string\n   167→  message: string\n   168→}\n   169→\n   170→const props = defineProps<{ form: Form<ContactForm> }>()\n   171→\n   172→const form = useLiveForm(() => props.form, {\n   173→  changeEvent: 'validate',\n   174→  submitEvent: 'submit'\n   175→})\n   176→\n   177→// Create typed field references\n   178→const nameField = form.field('name')\n   179→const emailField = form.field('email', { type: 'email' })\n   180→const subjectField = form.field('subject')\n   181→const messageField = form.field('message')\n   182→</script>\n   183→\n   184→<template>\n   185→  <div class=\"contact-form\">\n   186→    <div class=\"field\">\n   187→      <label :for=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Name</label>\n   188→      <input\n   189→        v-bind=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value\"\n   190→        :class=\"{ error: nameField.isTouched.value && nameField.errorMessage.value }\"\n   191→      />\n   192→      <div v-if=\"nameField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n   193→        {{ nameField.errorMessage.value }}\n   194→      </div>\n   195→    </div>\n   196→\n   197→    <div class=\"field\">\n   198→      <label :for=\"emailField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Email</label>\n   199→      <input\n   200→        v-bind=\"emailField.inputAttrs.value\"\n   201→        :class=\"{ error: emailField.isTouched.value && emailField.errorMessage.value }\"\n   202→      />\n   203→      <div v-if=\"emailField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n   204→        {{ emailField.errorMessage.value }}\n   205→      </div>\n   206→    </div>\n   207→\n   208→    <div class=\"field\">\n   209→      <label :for=\"subjectField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Subject</label>\n   210→      <input v-bind=\"subjectField.inputAttrs.value\" />\n   211→      <div v-if=\"subjectField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n   212→        {{ subjectField.errorMessage.value }}\n   213→      </div>\n   214→    </div>\n   215→\n   216→    <div class=\"field\">\n   217→      <label :for=\"messageField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Message</label>\n   218→      <textarea\n   219→        v-bind=\"messageField.inputAttrs.value\"\n   220→        rows=\"5\"\n   221→        :class=\"{ error: messageField.isTouched.value && messageField.errorMessage.value }\"\n   222→      />\n   223→      <div v-if=\"messageField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n   224→        {{ messageField.errorMessage.value }}\n   225→      </div>\n   226→    </div>\n   227→\n   228→    <div class=\"form-actions\">\n   229→      <button @click=\"form.reset()\" type=\"button\">Reset</button>\n   230→      <button\n   231→        @click=\"form.submit()\"\n   232→        :disabled=\"!form.isValid.value\"\n   233→        type=\"submit\"\n   234→      >\n   235→        Submit\n   236→      </button>\n   237→    </div>\n   238→\n   239→    <!-- Optional: Form state display -->\n   240→    <div class=\"form-status\">\n   241→      <p>Valid: {{ form.isValid.value }}</p>\n   242→      <p>Dirty: {{ form.isDirty.value }}</p>\n   243→      <p>Touched: {{ form.isTouched.value }}</p>\n   244→      <p>Validating: {{ form.isValidating.value }}</p>\n   245→    </div>\n   246→  </div>\n   247→</template>\n   248→```\n   249→\n   250→## API Reference\n   251→\n   252→### useLiveForm(form, options)\n   253→\n   254→Creates a reactive form instance with validation and state management.\n   255→\n   256→**Parameters:**\n   257→- `form` - Reactive reference to the form data from LiveView (typically `() => props.form`)\n   258→- `options` - Configuration object for form behavior\n   259→\n   260→**Options:**\n   261→\n   262→| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n   263→|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n   264→| `changeEvent` | `string \\| null` | `null` | Event sent on field changes (set to `null` to disable validation events) |\n   265→| `submitEvent` | `string` | `\"submit\"` | Event sent on form submission |\n   266→| `debounceInMiliseconds` | `number` | `300` | Debounce delay for change events to reduce server load |\n   267→| `prepareData` | `function` | `(data) => data` | Transform data before sending to server |\n   268→\n   269→**Returns:** [`UseLiveFormReturn<T>`](#useliveformreturn-interface)\n   270→\n   271→### Form Interface\n   272→\n   273→The form data structure passed from LiveView:\n   274→\n   275→| Property | Type | Description |\n   276→|----------|------|-------------|\n   277→| `name` | `string` | Form identifier (e.g., \"user\", \"contact\") |\n   278→| `values` | `T` | Current form values |\n   279→| `errors` | `object` | Validation errors from server (nested structure matching form shape) |\n   280→| `valid` | `boolean` | Whether the form is valid |\n   281→\n   282→### UseLiveFormReturn Interface\n   283→\n   284→The object returned by `useLiveForm()`:\n   285→\n   286→**Form-level state:**\n   287→\n   288→| Property | Type | Description |\n   289→|----------|------|-------------|\n   290→| `isValid` | `Ref<boolean>` | No validation errors exist |\n   291→| `isDirty` | `Ref<boolean>` | Form values differ from initial |\n   292→| `isTouched` | `Ref<boolean>` | At least one field has been interacted with |\n   293→| `isValidating` | `Readonly<Ref<boolean>>` | Whether validation requests are in progress (debounced or executing) |\n   294→| `submitCount` | `Readonly<Ref<number>>` | Number of submission attempts. Resets to 0 after successful submission |\n   295→| `initialValues` | `Readonly<Ref<T>>` | Original form values for reset |\n   296→\n   297→**Field factory functions:**\n   298→\n   299→| Method | Description |\n   300→|--------|-------------|\n   301→| `field(path, options?)` | Get a typed field instance for the given path (e.g., \"name\", \"user.email\", \"users[0].name\") with optional field configuration |\n   302→| `fieldArray(path)` | Get an array field instance for managing dynamic lists |\n   303→\n   304→**Form actions:**\n   305→\n   306→| Method | Description |\n   307→|--------|-------------|\n   308→| `submit()` | Submit form to server (returns Promise) |\n   309→| `reset()` | Reset to initial values and clear state |\n   310→\n   311→### FormField Interface\n   312→\n   313→Individual form field with reactive state and helpers:\n   314→\n   315→**Reactive state:**\n   316→\n   317→| Property | Type | Description |\n   318→|----------|------|-------------|\n   319→| `value` | `Ref<T>` | Current field value |\n   320→| `errors` | `Readonly<Ref<string[]>>` | Validation errors from server |\n   321→| `errorMessage` | `Readonly<Ref<string \\| undefined>>` | First error message |\n   322→| `isValid` | `Ref<boolean>` | No validation errors |\n   323→| `isDirty` | `Ref<boolean>` | Value differs from initial |\n   324→| `isTouched` | `Ref<boolean>` | Field has been blurred |\n   325→\n   326→**Input binding:**\n   327→\n   328→| Property | Description |\n   329→|----------|-------------|\n   330→| `inputAttrs` | Object containing `value`, event handlers (`onInput`, `onBlur`), `name`, `id`, and accessibility attributes (`aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`). Designed to be used with `v-bind` |\n   331→\n   332→**Navigation methods:**\n   333→\n   334→| Method | Description |\n   335→|--------|-------------|\n   336→| `field(key)` | Access nested object field |\n   337→| `fieldArray(key)` | Access nested array field |\n   338→\n   339→**Field actions:**\n   340→\n   341→| Method | Description |\n   342→|--------|-------------|\n   343→| `blur()` | Mark field as touched |\n   344→\n   345→### FormFieldArray Interface\n   346→\n   347→Array field with additional methods for array manipulation. If `changeEvent` is set, they will return a promise resolving when the item is validated through the server and added. Otherwise, promise resolves immediately.\n   348→\n   349→**Array operations:**\n   350→\n   351→| Method | Description |\n   352→|--------|-------------|\n   353→| `add(item?)` | Add new item to array (optionally with partial data). Returns a promise. |\n   354→| `remove(index)` | Remove item by index. Returns a promise. |\n   355→| `move(from, to)` | Move item to different position. Returns a promise. |\n   356→\n   357→\n   358→> #### Ecto by default removes empty values {: .tip}\n   359→>\n   360→> If calling `add()` on an array field does not add a new item, it often means that your Ecto changeset is filtering out empty or invalid values (e.g., empty strings in an array). Make sure your changeset doesn't consider value [you're trying to add as empty](https://hexdocs.pm/ecto/Ecto.Changeset.html#cast/4-options), or provide a valid initial value when adding.\n   361→\n   362→\n   363→**Reactive array:**\n   364→\n   365→| Property | Description |\n   366→|----------|-------------|\n   367→| `fields` | Array of field instances for iteration (`FormField<T>[]`) |\n   368→\n   369→**Individual array item access:**\n   370→\n   371→| Method | Description |\n   372→|--------|-------------|\n   373→| `field(path)` | Get individual array item fields (e.g., `field(0)`, `field('[0].name')`) |\n   374→| `fieldArray(path)` | Get nested array fields within array items |\n   375→\n   376→> **Note:** Array fields inherit all properties and methods from `FormField` except `field()` and `fieldArray()` navigation methods, which are replaced with array-specific versions.\n   377→\n   378→### Field Options\n   379→\n   380→When creating fields, you can pass an optional `options` parameter to configure field behavior:\n   381→\n   382→```typescript\n   383→interface FieldOptions {\n   384→  type?: string     // HTML input type (e.g., \"email\", \"password\", \"checkbox\")\n   385→  value?: any       // For checkbox/radio: the value this field represents when selected\n   386→}\n   387→```\n   388→\n   389→**Examples:**\n   390→\n   391→```javascript\n   392→// Basic field (infers type from data)\n   393→const nameField = form.field('name')\n   394→\n   395→// Email input with validation\n   396→const emailField = form.field('email', { type: 'email' })\n   397→\n   398→// Password input\n   399→const passwordField = form.field('password', { type: 'password' })\n   400→\n   401→// Boolean checkbox\n   402→const acceptTerms = form.field('acceptTerms', { type: 'checkbox' })\n   403→\n   404→// Single checkbox with custom value\n   405→const planField = form.field('plan', { type: 'checkbox', value: 'premium' })\n   406→\n   407→// Multiple checkboxes (automatically detected when same field has different values)\n   408→const emailPrefs = form.field('preferences', { type: 'checkbox', value: 'email' })\n   409→const smsPrefs = form.field('preferences', { type: 'checkbox', value: 'sms' })\n   410→```\n   411→\n   412→## Working with Fields\n   413→\n   414→### Field State\n   415→\n   416→Each field provides reactive state that updates automatically:\n   417→\n   418→```html\n   419→<script setup>\n   420→const nameField = form.field('name')\n   421→\n   422→// Reactive field state\n   423→console.log(nameField.value.value)        // Current value\n   424→console.log(nameField.errors.value)       // Array of error strings\n   425→console.log(nameField.errorMessage.value) // First error or undefined\n   426→console.log(nameField.isValid.value)      // true if no errors\n   427→console.log(nameField.isDirty.value)      // true if changed from initial\n   428→console.log(nameField.isTouched.value)    // true if user interacted\n   429→</script>\n   430→\n   431→<template>\n   432→  <!-- Display field state -->\n   433→  <div class=\"field-debug\">\n   434→    <p>Value: {{ nameField.value.value }}</p>\n   435→    <p>Valid: {{ nameField.isValid.value }}</p>\n   436→    <p>Dirty: {{ nameField.isDirty.value }}</p>\n   437→    <p>Touched: {{ nameField.isTouched.value }}</p>\n   438→    <p>Errors: {{ nameField.errors.value }}</p>\n   439→  </div>\n   440→</template>\n   441→```\n   442→\n   443→### Input Binding\n   444→\n   445→The `inputAttrs` property provides all necessary attributes for form inputs:\n   446→\n   447→```html\n   448→<template>\n   449→  <!-- Automatic binding with all attributes -->\n   450→  <input v-bind=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value\" />\n   451→\n   452→  <!-- Manual binding (equivalent to above) -->\n   453→  <input\n   454→    :value=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value.value\"\n   455→    @input=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value.onInput\"\n   456→    @blur=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value.onBlur\"\n   457→    :name=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value.name\"\n   458→    :id=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value.id\"\n   459→    :aria-invalid=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value['aria-invalid']\"\n   460→    :aria-describedby=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value['aria-describedby']\"\n   461→  />\n   462→\n   463→  <!-- Error message with proper ID linking -->\n   464→  <div\n   465→    v-if=\"nameField.errorMessage.value\"\n   466→    :id=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value.id + '-error'\"\n   467→    class=\"error\"\n   468→  >\n   469→    {{ nameField.errorMessage.value }}\n   470→  </div>\n   471→</template>\n   472→```\n   473→\n   474→### Custom Field Components\n   475→\n   476→Create reusable field components by extracting the binding logic:\n   477→\n   478→```html\n   479→<!-- TextInput.vue -->\n   480→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n   481→interface Props {\n   482→  field: FormField<string>\n   483→  label: string\n   484→  type?: string\n   485→  placeholder?: string\n   486→}\n   487→\n   488→const props = withDefaults(defineProps<Props>(), {\n   489→  type: 'text'\n   490→})\n   491→</script>\n   492→\n   493→<template>\n   494→  <div class=\"field\">\n   495→    <label :for=\"field.inputAttrs.value.id\">{{ label }}</label>\n   496→    <input\n   497→      v-bind=\"field.inputAttrs.value\"\n   498→      :type=\"type\"\n   499→      :placeholder=\"placeholder\"\n   500→      :class=\"{ error: field.isTouched.value && field.errorMessage.value }\"\n   501→    />\n   502→    <div v-if=\"field.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n   503→      {{ field.errorMessage.value }}\n   504→    </div>\n   505→  </div>\n   506→</template>\n   507→```\n   508→\n   509→Usage:\n   510→```html\n   511→<TextInput :field=\"form.field('name')\" label=\"Full Name\" placeholder=\"Enter your name\" />\n   512→<TextInput :field=\"form.field('email', { type: 'email' })\" label=\"Email\" />\n   513→```\n   514→\n   515→### Checkbox Fields\n   516→\n   517→LiveVue supports three checkbox patterns that automatically handle different use cases:\n   518→\n   519→#### 1. Boolean Checkbox\n   520→\n   521→For simple true/false fields:\n   522→\n   523→```html\n   524→<script setup>\n   525→const acceptTerms = form.field('acceptTerms', { type: 'checkbox' })\n   526→</script>\n   527→\n   528→<template>\n   529→  <label>\n   530→    <input v-bind=\"acceptTerms.inputAttrs.value\" />\n   531→    I accept the terms and conditions\n   532→  </label>\n   533→</template>\n   534→```\n   535→\n   536→#### 2. Single Checkbox with Custom Value\n   537→\n   538→For fields that should have a specific value when checked:\n   539→\n   540→```html\n   541→<script setup>\n   542→const plan = form.field('plan', { type: 'checkbox', value: 'premium' })\n   543→</script>\n   544→\n   545→<template>\n   546→  <label>\n   547→    <input v-bind=\"plan.inputAttrs.value\" />\n   548→    Upgrade to Premium ($9.99/month)\n   549→  </label>\n   550→  <!-- When checked: plan.value = 'premium', when unchecked: plan.value = null -->\n   551→</template>\n   552→```\n   553→\n   554→#### 3. Multiple Checkboxes (Array)\n   555→\n   556→When you create multiple checkboxes for the same field path with different values, LiveVue automatically detects this as a multi-checkbox scenario and manages an array:\n   557→\n   558→```html\n   559→<script setup>\n   560→// These automatically become array-aware\n   561→const emailPref = form.field('preferences', { type: 'checkbox', value: 'email' })\n   562→const smsPref = form.field('preferences', { type: 'checkbox', value: 'sms' })\n   563→const pushPref = form.field('preferences', { type: 'checkbox', value: 'push' })\n   564→</script>\n   565→\n   566→<template>\n   567→  <fieldset>\n   568→    <legend>Notification Preferences</legend>\n   569→    \n   570→    <label>\n   571→      <input v-bind=\"emailPref.inputAttrs.value\" />\n   572→      Email notifications\n   573→    </label>\n   574→    \n   575→    <label>\n   576→      <input v-bind=\"smsPref.inputAttrs.value\" />\n   577→      SMS notifications  \n   578→    </label>\n   579→    \n   580→    <label>\n   581→      <input v-bind=\"pushPref.inputAttrs.value\" />\n   582→      Push notifications\n   583→    </label>\n   584→  </fieldset>\n   585→  <!-- When checked, values are added/removed from the array automatically -->\n   586→  <!-- e.g., preferences.value = ['email', 'push'] -->\n   587→</template>\n   588→```\n   589→\n   590→The checkbox behavior is automatically determined by:\n   591→- **Boolean**: `type: 'checkbox'` without `value` option\n   592→- **Single with value**: `type: 'checkbox'` with `value` option  \n   593→- **Multiple**: Same field path used with different `value` options\n   594→\n   595→## Nested Fields\n   596→\n   597→### Object Navigation\n   598→\n   599→Access nested object fields using dot notation:\n   600→\n   601→```typescript\n   602→type UserProfile = {\n   603→  name: string\n   604→  email: string\n   605→  address: {\n   606→    street: string\n   607→    city: string\n   608→    country: string\n   609→  }\n   610→  preferences: {\n   611→    newsletter: boolean\n   612→    theme: 'light' | 'dark'\n   613→    notifications: {\n   614→      email: boolean\n   615→      push: boolean\n   616→    }\n   617→  }\n   618→}\n   619→\n   620→const form = useLiveForm<UserProfile>(/* ... */)\n   621→\n   622→// Access nested fields with full type safety\n   623→const nameField = form.field('name')                           // FormField<string>\n   624→const streetField = form.field('address.street')               // FormField<string>\n   625→const themeField = form.field('preferences.theme')             // FormField<'light' | 'dark'>\n   626→const emailNotifField = form.field('preferences.notifications.email') // FormField<boolean>\n   627→```\n   628→\n   629→### Fluent Field Navigation\n   630→\n   631→You can also navigate through object structures using the field methods:\n   632→\n   633→```typescript\n   634→// Equivalent ways to access nested fields\n   635→const emailNotifField1 = form.field('preferences.notifications.email')\n   636→\n   637→const preferencesField = form.field('preferences')\n   638→const notificationsField = preferencesField.field('notifications')\n   639→const emailNotifField2 = notificationsField.field('email')\n   640→\n   641→// Both approaches are type-safe and equivalent\n   642→```\n   643→\n   644→### Complex Nested Structures\n   645→\n   646→```html\n   647→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n   648→type CompanyForm = {\n   649→  name: string\n   650→  headquarters: {\n   651→    address: {\n   652→      street: string\n   653→      city: string\n   654→      postal_code: string\n   655→    }\n   656→    contact: {\n   657→      phone: string\n   658→      email: string\n   659→    }\n   660→  }\n   661→  departments: Array<{\n   662→    name: string\n   663→    manager: {\n   664→      name: string\n   665→      email: string\n   666→    }\n   667→  }>\n   668→}\n   669→\n   670→const form = useLiveForm<CompanyForm>(/* ... */)\n   671→\n   672→// Access deeply nested fields\n   673→const companyNameField = form.field('name')\n   674→const hqStreetField = form.field('headquarters.address.street')\n   675→const hqPhoneField = form.field('headquarters.contact.phone')\n   676→const departmentsArray = form.fieldArray('departments')\n   677→</script>\n   678→\n   679→<template>\n   680→  <div>\n   681→    <!-- Company basic info -->\n   682→    <TextInput :field=\"companyNameField\" label=\"Company Name\" />\n   683→\n   684→    <!-- Headquarters address -->\n   685→    <fieldset>\n   686→      <legend>Headquarters</legend>\n   687→      <TextInput :field=\"hqStreetField\" label=\"Street\" />\n   688→      <TextInput :field=\"form.field('headquarters.address.city')\" label=\"City\" />\n   689→      <TextInput :field=\"form.field('headquarters.address.postal_code')\" label=\"Postal Code\" />\n   690→      <TextInput :field=\"hqPhoneField\" label=\"Phone\" />\n   691→      <TextInput :field=\"form.field('headquarters.contact.email')\" label=\"Email\" type=\"email\" />\n   692→    </fieldset>\n   693→\n   694→    <!-- Departments array -->\n   695→    <fieldset>\n   696→      <legend>Departments</legend>\n   697→      <div v-for=\"(deptField, index) in departmentsArray.fields.value\" :key=\"index\">\n   698→        <h4>Department {{ index + 1 }}</h4>\n   699→        <TextInput :field=\"deptField.field('name')\" label=\"Department Name\" />\n   700→        <TextInput :field=\"deptField.field('manager.name')\" label=\"Manager Name\" />\n   701→        <TextInput :field=\"deptField.field('manager.email')\" label=\"Manager Email\" type=\"email\" />\n   702→        <button @click=\"departmentsArray.remove(index)\">Remove Department</button>\n   703→      </div>\n   704→      <button @click=\"departmentsArray.add({ name: '', manager: { name: '', email: '' } })\">\n   705→        Add Department\n   706→      </button>\n   707→    </fieldset>\n   708→  </div>\n   709→</template>\n   710→```\n   711→\n   712→## Array Fields\n   713→\n   714→### Basic Array Operations\n   715→\n   716→Array fields provide methods for adding, removing, and reordering items:\n   717→\n   718→```html\n   719→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n   720→type TagsForm = {\n   721→  title: string\n   722→  tags: string[]\n   723→}\n   724→\n   725→const form = useLiveForm<TagsForm>(/* ... */)\n   726→const titleField = form.field('title')\n   727→const tagsArray = form.fieldArray('tags')\n   728→\n   729→// Array operations\n   730→const addTag = () => tagsArray.add('')\n   731→const removeTag = (index: number) => tagsArray.remove(index)\n   732→const moveTag = (from: number, to: number) => tagsArray.move(from, to)\n   733→</script>\n   734→\n   735→<template>\n   736→  <div>\n   737→    <TextInput :field=\"titleField\" label=\"Title\" />\n   738→\n   739→    <!-- Tags array -->\n   740→    <fieldset>\n   741→      <legend>Tags</legend>\n   742→      <div v-for=\"(tagField, index) in tagsArray.fields.value\" :key=\"index\" class=\"tag-item\">\n   743→        <input v-bind=\"tagField.inputAttrs.value\" placeholder=\"Enter tag\" />\n   744→        <button @click=\"removeTag(index)\">Remove</button>\n   745→        <button v-if=\"index > 0\" @click=\"moveTag(index, index - 1)\">↑</button>\n   746→        <button v-if=\"index < tagsArray.fields.value.length - 1\" @click=\"moveTag(index, index + 1)\">↓</button>\n   747→      </div>\n   748→      <button @click=\"addTag()\">Add Tag</button>\n   749→    </fieldset>\n   750→  </div>\n   751→</template>\n   752→```\n   753→\n   754→### Array Field Indexing\n   755→\n   756→Access individual array items using multiple syntaxes:\n   757→\n   758→```typescript\n   759→const skillsArray = form.fieldArray('profile.skills')\n   760→\n   761→// Method 1: Using numeric index\n   762→const firstSkill = skillsArray.field(0)                    // FormField<string>\n   763→\n   764→// Method 2: Using bracket notation\n   765→const secondSkill = skillsArray.field('[1]')               // FormField<string>\n   766→\n   767→// Method 3: Using the fields array (for iteration)\n   768→const allSkillFields = skillsArray.fields.value            // FormField<string>[]\n   769→```\n   770→\n   771→### Complex Array Structures\n   772→\n   773→Handle arrays of objects with nested properties:\n   774→\n   775→```html\n   776→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n   777→type ProjectForm = {\n   778→  name: string\n   779→  team_members: Array<{\n   780→    name: string\n   781→    email: string\n   782→    role: string\n   783→    skills: string[]\n   784→    contact: {\n   785→      phone: string\n   786→      address: string\n   787→    }\n   788→  }>\n   789→}\n   790→\n   791→const form = useLiveForm<ProjectForm>(/* ... */)\n   792→const membersArray = form.fieldArray('team_members')\n   793→\n   794→const addMember = () => {\n   795→  membersArray.add({\n   796→    name: '',\n   797→    email: '',\n   798→    role: 'developer',\n   799→    skills: [],\n   800→    contact: { phone: '', address: '' }\n   801→  })\n   802→}\n   803→\n   804→const addSkillToMember = (memberIndex: number) => {\n   805→  const memberField = membersArray.field(memberIndex)\n   806→  const skillsArray = memberField.fieldArray('skills')\n   807→  skillsArray.add('')\n   808→}\n   809→</script>\n   810→\n   811→<template>\n   812→  <div>\n   813→    <TextInput :field=\"form.field('name')\" label=\"Project Name\" />\n   814→\n   815→    <fieldset>\n   816→      <legend>Team Members</legend>\n   817→      <div v-for=\"(memberField, memberIndex) in membersArray.fields.value\" :key=\"memberIndex\" class=\"member-card\">\n   818→        <h4>Member {{ memberIndex + 1 }}</h4>\n   819→\n   820→        <!-- Basic member info -->\n   821→        <TextInput :field=\"memberField.field('name')\" label=\"Name\" />\n   822→        <TextInput :field=\"memberField.field('email')\" label=\"Email\" type=\"email\" />\n   823→        <select v-bind=\"memberField.field('role').inputAttrs.value\">\n   824→          <option value=\"developer\">Developer</option>\n   825→          <option value=\"designer\">Designer</option>\n   826→          <option value=\"manager\">Manager</option>\n   827→        </select>\n   828→\n   829→        <!-- Contact info (nested object) -->\n   830→        <fieldset>\n   831→          <legend>Contact Information</legend>\n   832→          <TextInput :field=\"memberField.field('contact.phone')\" label=\"Phone\" />\n   833→          <TextInput :field=\"memberField.field('contact.address')\" label=\"Address\" />\n   834→        </fieldset>\n   835→\n   836→        <!-- Skills array (nested array) -->\n   837→        <fieldset>\n   838→          <legend>Skills</legend>\n   839→          <div\n   840→            v-for=\"(skillField, skillIndex) in memberField.fieldArray('skills').fields.value\"\n   841→            :key=\"skillIndex\"\n   842→            class=\"skill-item\"\n   843→          >\n   844→            <input v-bind=\"skillField.inputAttrs.value\" placeholder=\"Enter skill\" />\n   845→            <button @click=\"memberField.fieldArray('skills').remove(skillIndex)\">Remove</button>\n   846→          </div>\n   847→          <button @click=\"addSkillToMember(memberIndex)\">Add Skill</button>\n   848→        </fieldset>\n   849→\n   850→        <button @click=\"membersArray.remove(memberIndex)\">Remove Member</button>\n   851→      </div>\n   852→\n   853→      <button @click=\"addMember()\">Add Team Member</button>\n   854→    </fieldset>\n   855→  </div>\n   856→</template>\n   857→```\n   858→\n   859→### Deeply Nested Arrays\n   860→\n   861→Handle arrays within arrays within objects:\n   862→\n   863→```typescript\n   864→type BlogPost = {\n   865→  title: string\n   866→  sections: Array<{\n   867→    heading: string\n   868→    paragraphs: string[]\n   869→    comments: Array<{\n   870→      author: string\n   871→      text: string\n   872→      replies: Array<{\n   873→        author: string\n   874→        text: string\n   875→      }>\n   876→    }>\n   877→  }>\n   878→}\n   879→\n   880→const form = useLiveForm<BlogPost>(/* ... */)\n   881→\n   882→// Access deeply nested arrays\n   883→const sectionsArray = form.fieldArray('sections')\n   884→const firstSectionParagraphs = sectionsArray.field('[0].paragraphs')  // FormFieldArray<string>\n   885→const firstSectionComments = sectionsArray.field('[0].comments')      // FormFieldArray<Comment>\n   886→\n   887→// Using fluent interface\n   888→const firstSection = sectionsArray.field(0)                           // FormField<Section>\n   889→const firstSectionParagraphsAlt = firstSection.fieldArray('paragraphs') // FormFieldArray<string>\n   890→\n   891→// Access replies of first comment in first section\n   892→const firstCommentReplies = sectionsArray.fieldArray('[0].comments').field('[0].replies') // FormFieldArray<Reply>\n   893→```\n   894→\n   895→## Form State Management\n   896→\n   897→### Form-Level State\n   898→\n   899→The form instance provides reactive state about the entire form:\n   900→\n   901→```html\n   902→<script setup>\n   903→const form = useLiveForm(/* ... */)\n   904→\n   905→// Form state is reactive\n   906→watch(() => form.isValid.value, (valid) => {\n   907→  console.log('Form validity changed:', valid)\n   908→})\n   909→\n   910→watch(() => form.isDirty.value, (dirty) => {\n   911→  if (dirty) {\n   912→    console.log('Form has unsaved changes')\n   913→  }\n   914→})\n   915→\n   916→watch(() => form.isValidating.value, (validating) => {\n   917→  console.log('Validation status:', validating ? 'in progress' : 'complete')\n   918→})\n   919→</script>\n   920→\n   921→<template>\n   922→  <div class=\"form-status\">\n   923→    <!-- Visual indicators -->\n   924→    <div :class=\"{ 'status-valid': form.isValid.value, 'status-invalid': !form.isValid.value }\">\n   925→      {{ form.isValid.value ? '✓ Valid' : '✗ Has Errors' }}\n   926→    </div>\n   927→\n   928→    <div :class=\"{ 'status-dirty': form.isDirty.value }\">\n   929→      {{ form.isDirty.value ? '● Unsaved Changes' : '✓ Saved' }}\n   930→    </div>\n   931→\n   932→    <div v-if=\"form.isTouched.value\">\n   933→      User has interacted with the form\n   934→    </div>\n   935→\n   936→    <div v-if=\"form.isValidating.value\" class=\"validating\">\n   937→      🔄 Validating changes...\n   938→    </div>\n   939→\n   940→    <div>\n   941→      Submit attempts: {{ form.submitCount.value }}\n   942→    </div>\n   943→  </div>\n   944→\n   945→  <!-- Conditional submit button -->\n   946→  <button\n   947→    @click=\"form.submit()\"\n   948→    :disabled=\"!form.isValid.value || !form.isDirty.value || form.isValidating.value\"\n   949→    class=\"submit-btn\"\n   950→  >\n   951→    {{ form.isValidating.value ? 'Validating...' : form.isDirty.value ? 'Save Changes' : 'No Changes' }}\n   952→  </button>\n   953→</template>\n   954→```\n   955→\n   956→### Reset and Submit Actions\n   957→\n   958→```html\n   959→<script setup>\n   960→const form = useLiveForm(/* ... */)\n   961→\n   962→const handleSubmit = async () => {\n   963→  try {\n   964→    await form.submit()\n   965→    console.log('Form submitted successfully!')\n   966→    // Form will automatically reset on successful submission\n   967→  } catch (error) {\n   968→    console.error('Submission failed:', error)\n   969→    // Form state remains intact for user to fix errors\n   970→  }\n   971→}\n   972→\n   973→const handleReset = () => {\n   974→  if (form.isDirty.value) {\n   975→    if (confirm('You have unsaved changes. Are you sure you want to reset?')) {\n   976→      form.reset()\n   977→    }\n   978→  } else {\n   979→    form.reset()\n   980→  }\n   981→}\n   982→\n   983→const handleCancel = () => {\n   984→  // Navigate away or close modal\n   985→  if (form.isDirty.value) {\n   986→    if (confirm('You have unsaved changes. Are you sure you want to cancel?')) {\n   987→      // Navigate away\n   988→      $live.pushEvent('cancel')\n   989→    }\n   990→  }\n   991→}\n   992→</script>\n   993→\n   994→<template>\n   995→  <div class=\"form-actions\">\n   996→    <button @click=\"handleReset\" type=\"button\" :disabled=\"!form.isDirty.value\">\n   997→      Reset\n   998→    </button>\n   999→    <button @click=\"handleCancel\" type=\"button\">\n  1000→      Cancel\n  1001→    </button>\n  1002→    <button @click=\"handleSubmit\" :disabled=\"!form.isValid.value\">\n  1003→      {{ form.submitCount.value > 0 ? 'Resubmit' : 'Submit' }}\n  1004→    </button>\n  1005→  </div>\n  1006→</template>\n  1007→```\n  1008→\n  1009→## Advanced Patterns\n  1010→\n  1011→### Custom Validation Logic\n  1012→\n  1013→While server-side validation is primary, you can add client-side validation for better UX:\n  1014→\n  1015→```html\n  1016→<script setup>\n  1017→const form = useLiveForm(/* ... */)\n  1018→const emailField = form.field('email')\n  1019→const passwordField = form.field('password')\n  1020→const confirmPasswordField = form.field('confirm_password')\n  1021→\n  1022→// Client-side validation helpers\n  1023→const emailIsValid = computed(() => {\n  1024→  const value = emailField.value.value\n  1025→  return !value || /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/.test(value)\n  1026→})\n  1027→\n  1028→const passwordsMatch = computed(() => {\n  1029→  return passwordField.value.value === confirmPasswordField.value.value\n  1030→})\n  1031→\n  1032→// Combine client and server validation\n  1033→const emailHasError = computed(() => {\n  1034→  return (emailField.isTouched.value && !emailIsValid.value) ||\n  1035→         (emailField.errorMessage.value !== undefined)\n  1036→})\n  1037→</script>\n  1038→\n  1039→<template>\n  1040→  <div class=\"field\">\n  1041→    <input\n  1042→      v-bind=\"emailField.inputAttrs.value\"\n  1043→      type=\"email\"\n  1044→      :class=\"{ error: emailHasError.value }\"\n  1045→    />\n  1046→    <!-- Show client-side error first, then server error -->\n  1047→    <div v-if=\"emailField.isTouched.value && !emailIsValid.value\" class=\"error\">\n  1048→      Please enter a valid email address\n  1049→    </div>\n  1050→    <div v-else-if=\"emailField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error\">\n  1051→      {{ emailField.errorMessage.value }}\n  1052→    </div>\n  1053→  </div>\n  1054→\n  1055→  <div class=\"field\">\n  1056→    <input v-bind=\"confirmPasswordField.inputAttrs.value\" type=\"password\" />\n  1057→    <div v-if=\"confirmPasswordField.isTouched.value && !passwordsMatch.value\" class=\"error\">\n  1058→      Passwords do not match\n  1059→    </div>\n  1060→  </div>\n  1061→</template>\n  1062→```\n  1063→\n  1064→### Data Transformation\n  1065→\n  1066→Transform form data before sending to the server. The `prepareData` function is applied to form data before **both** `changeEvent` (validation) and `submitEvent` (submission) requests, ensuring consistent data transformation for all server communication:\n  1067→\n  1068→```html\n  1069→<script setup>\n  1070→type RawForm = {\n  1071→  name: string\n  1072→  tags: string\n  1073→  price: string\n  1074→  is_active: string\n  1075→}\n  1076→\n  1077→type ProcessedForm = {\n  1078→  name: string\n  1079→  tags: string[]\n  1080→  price: number\n  1081→  is_active: boolean\n  1082→}\n  1083→\n  1084→const form = useLiveForm<RawForm>(() => props.form, {\n  1085→  changeEvent: 'validate',\n  1086→  submitEvent: 'submit',\n  1087→  prepareData: (data: RawForm): ProcessedForm => {\n  1088→    return {\n  1089→      name: data.name.trim(),\n  1090→      tags: data.tags.split(',').map(tag => tag.trim()).filter(Boolean),\n  1091→      price: parseFloat(data.price) || 0,\n  1092→      is_active: data.is_active === 'true'\n  1093→    }\n  1094→  }\n  1095→})\n  1096→\n  1097→// Form fields work with the raw format\n  1098→const tagsField = form.field('tags')  // string field for comma-separated input\n  1099→const priceField = form.field('price')  // string field for user input\n  1100→</script>\n  1101→\n  1102→<template>\n  1103→  <!-- User enters comma-separated tags -->\n  1104→  <input v-bind=\"tagsField.inputAttrs.value\" placeholder=\"javascript, vue, forms\" />\n  1105→\n  1106→  <!-- User enters price as string -->\n  1107→  <input v-bind=\"priceField.inputAttrs.value\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.01\" />\n  1108→</template>\n  1109→```\n  1110→\n  1111→### Conditional Field Logic\n  1112→\n  1113→Show/hide fields based on form state:\n  1114→\n  1115→```html\n  1116→<script setup>\n  1117→type UserForm = {\n  1118→  account_type: 'personal' | 'business'\n  1119→  name: string\n  1120→  company_name?: string\n  1121→  tax_id?: string\n  1122→  billing_address: string\n  1123→  shipping_address?: string\n  1124→  same_as_billing: boolean\n  1125→}\n  1126→\n  1127→const form = useLiveForm<UserForm>(/* ... */)\n  1128→\n  1129→const accountTypeField = form.field('account_type')\n  1130→const sameAsBillingField = form.field('same_as_billing')\n  1131→\n  1132→const isBusinessAccount = computed(() =>\n  1133→  accountTypeField.value.value === 'business'\n  1134→)\n  1135→\n  1136→const needsShippingAddress = computed(() =>\n  1137→  !sameAsBillingField.value.value\n  1138→)\n  1139→\n  1140→// Clear conditional fields when they become hidden\n  1141→watch(isBusinessAccount, (isBusiness) => {\n  1142→  if (!isBusiness) {\n  1143→    form.field('company_name').value.value = ''\n  1144→    form.field('tax_id').value.value = ''\n  1145→  }\n  1146→})\n  1147→\n  1148→watch(needsShippingAddress, (needsShipping) => {\n  1149→  if (!needsShipping) {\n  1150→    form.field('shipping_address').value.value = ''\n  1151→  }\n  1152→})\n  1153→</script>\n  1154→\n  1155→<template>\n  1156→  <div>\n  1157→    <select v-bind=\"accountTypeField.inputAttrs.value\">\n  1158→      <option value=\"personal\">Personal</option>\n  1159→      <option value=\"business\">Business</option>\n  1160→    </select>\n  1161→\n  1162→    <!-- Business-only fields -->\n  1163→    <div v-if=\"isBusinessAccount\">\n  1164→      <TextInput :field=\"form.field('company_name')\" label=\"Company Name\" />\n  1165→      <TextInput :field=\"form.field('tax_id')\" label=\"Tax ID\" />\n  1166→    </div>\n  1167→\n  1168→    <TextInput :field=\"form.field('billing_address')\" label=\"Billing Address\" />\n  1169→\n  1170→    <label>\n  1171→      <input type=\"checkbox\" v-bind=\"sameAsBillingField.inputAttrs.value\" />\n  1172→      Shipping address same as billing\n  1173→    </label>\n  1174→\n  1175→    <div v-if=\"needsShippingAddress\">\n  1176→      <TextInput :field=\"form.field('shipping_address')\" label=\"Shipping Address\" />\n  1177→    </div>\n  1178→  </div>\n  1179→</template>\n  1180→```\n  1181→\n  1182→## Provide/Inject API (Advanced)\n  1183→\n  1184→For building reusable form components, LiveVue provides `useField()` and `useArrayField()` hooks that work with Vue's provide/inject system.\n  1185→\n  1186→> #### Advanced API {: .warning}\n  1187→>\n  1188→> This is an advanced pattern for creating reusable form components. Most applications should use the direct field access patterns shown above.\n  1189→\n  1190→### Component Injection\n  1191→\n  1192→When you call `useLiveForm()`, it automatically provides the form instance to child components:\n  1193→\n  1194→```html\n  1195→<!-- ParentForm.vue -->\n  1196→<script setup>\n  1197→const form = useLiveForm(/* ... */)\n  1198→// Form instance is automatically provided to children\n  1199→</script>\n  1200→\n  1201→<template>\n  1202→  <div>\n  1203→    <!-- These child components can access form fields -->\n  1204→    <UserNameInput />\n  1205→    <UserEmailInput />\n  1206→    <SkillsManager />\n  1207→  </div>\n  1208→</template>\n  1209→```\n  1210→\n  1211→### useField Hook\n  1212→\n  1213→Create reusable field components that access the parent form:\n  1214→\n  1215→```html\n  1216→<!-- UserNameInput.vue -->\n  1217→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n  1218→import { useField } from 'live_vue'\n  1219→\n  1220→interface Props {\n  1221→  path?: string\n  1222→}\n  1223→\n  1224→const props = withDefaults(defineProps<Props>(), {\n  1225→  path: 'name'\n  1226→})\n  1227→\n  1228→// Access field from parent form context\n  1229→const field = useField<string>(props.path)\n  1230→</script>\n  1231→\n  1232→<template>\n  1233→  <div class=\"field\">\n  1234→    <label :for=\"field.inputAttrs.value.id\">Full Name</label>\n  1235→    <input\n  1236→      v-bind=\"field.inputAttrs.value\"\n  1237→      :class=\"{ error: field.isTouched.value && field.errorMessage.value }\"\n  1238→      placeholder=\"Enter your full name\"\n  1239→    />\n  1240→    <div v-if=\"field.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n  1241→      {{ field.errorMessage.value }}\n  1242→    </div>\n  1243→  </div>\n  1244→</template>\n  1245→```\n  1246→\n  1247→### useArrayField Hook\n  1248→\n  1249→Create reusable array field managers:\n  1250→\n  1251→```html\n  1252→<!-- SkillsManager.vue -->\n  1253→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n  1254→import { useArrayField } from 'live_vue'\n  1255→\n  1256→interface Props {\n  1257→  path?: string\n  1258→}\n  1259→\n  1260→const props = withDefaults(defineProps<Props>(), {\n  1261→  path: 'skills'\n  1262→})\n  1263→\n  1264→const skillsArray = useArrayField<string>(props.path)\n  1265→\n  1266→const addSkill = () => skillsArray.add('')\n  1267→const removeSkill = (index: number) => skillsArray.remove(index)\n  1268→</script>\n  1269→\n  1270→<template>\n  1271→  <fieldset>\n  1272→    <legend>Skills</legend>\n  1273→\n  1274→    <div v-for=\"(skillField, index) in skillsArray.fields.value\" :key=\"index\" class=\"skill-item\">\n  1275→      <input v-bind=\"skillField.inputAttrs.value\" placeholder=\"Enter skill\" />\n  1276→      <button @click=\"removeSkill(index)\" type=\"button\">Remove</button>\n  1277→    </div>\n  1278→\n  1279→    <button @click=\"addSkill\" type=\"button\">Add Skill</button>\n  1280→\n  1281→    <div v-if=\"skillsArray.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n  1282→      {{ skillsArray.errorMessage.value }}\n  1283→    </div>\n  1284→  </fieldset>\n  1285→</template>\n  1286→```\n  1287→\n  1288→### Complex Reusable Components\n  1289→\n  1290→Build sophisticated reusable form sections:\n  1291→\n  1292→```html\n  1293→<!-- AddressInput.vue -->\n  1294→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n  1295→import { useField } from 'live_vue'\n  1296→\n  1297→interface Props {\n  1298→  basePath: string      // e.g., 'billing_address' or 'shipping_address'\n  1299→  label: string\n  1300→}\n  1301→\n  1302→const props = defineProps<Props>()\n  1303→\n  1304→// Access nested address fields\n  1305→const streetField = useField<string>(`${props.basePath}.street`)\n  1306→const cityField = useField<string>(`${props.basePath}.city`)\n  1307→const stateField = useField<string>(`${props.basePath}.state`)\n  1308→const zipField = useField<string>(`${props.basePath}.zip`)\n  1309→const countryField = useField<string>(`${props.basePath}.country`)\n  1310→</script>\n  1311→\n  1312→<template>\n  1313→  <fieldset>\n  1314→    <legend>{{ label }}</legend>\n  1315→\n  1316→    <div class=\"address-grid\">\n  1317→      <TextInput :field=\"streetField\" label=\"Street Address\" />\n  1318→      <TextInput :field=\"cityField\" label=\"City\" />\n  1319→      <TextInput :field=\"stateField\" label=\"State\" />\n  1320→      <TextInput :field=\"zipField\" label=\"ZIP Code\" />\n  1321→\n  1322→      <div class=\"field\">\n  1323→        <label :for=\"countryField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Country</label>\n  1324→        <select v-bind=\"countryField.inputAttrs.value\">\n  1325→          <option value=\"US\">United States</option>\n  1326→          <option value=\"CA\">Canada</option>\n  1327→          <option value=\"UK\">United Kingdom</option>\n  1328→        </select>\n  1329→      </div>\n  1330→    </div>\n  1331→  </fieldset>\n  1332→</template>\n  1333→```\n  1334→\n  1335→Usage:\n  1336→```html\n  1337→<template>\n  1338→  <div>\n  1339→    <AddressInput base-path=\"billing_address\" label=\"Billing Address\" />\n  1340→    <AddressInput base-path=\"shipping_address\" label=\"Shipping Address\" />\n  1341→  </div>\n  1342→</template>\n  1343→```\n  1344→\n  1345→### Error Handling with Inject\n  1346→\n  1347→```html\n  1348→<!-- Component using injection -->\n  1349→<script setup>\n  1350→import { useField, useArrayField } from 'live_vue'\n  1351→\n  1352→// These composables require a parent component that called useLiveForm()\n  1353→const nameField = useField('name')\n  1354→const skillsArray = useArrayField('skills')\n  1355→</script>\n  1356→```\n  1357→\n  1358→If `useField()` or `useArrayField()` are used outside a form context (i.e., not in a child component of one that called `useLiveForm()`), they will throw an error:\n  1359→\n  1360→```\n  1361→useField() can only be used inside components where a form has been provided.\n  1362→Make sure a parent component calls useLiveForm() first.\n  1363→```\n  1364→\n  1365→This error indicates you need to either:\n  1366→1. Call `useLiveForm()` in a parent component, or\n  1367→2. Use the `form.field()` method directly instead of `useField()`\n  1368→\n  1369→## Server-Side Integration\n  1370→\n  1371→### Ecto Changeset Integration\n  1372→\n  1373→LiveVue forms work seamlessly with Ecto changesets:\n  1374→\n  1375→```elixir\n  1376→defmodule MyApp.User do\n  1377→  use Ecto.Schema\n  1378→  import Ecto.Changeset\n  1379→\n  1380→  schema \"users\" do\n  1381→    field :name, :string\n  1382→    field :email, :string\n  1383→    field :age, :integer\n  1384→\n  1385→    embeds_one :profile, Profile do\n  1386→      field :bio, :string\n  1387→      field :skills, {:array, :string}, default: []\n  1388→    end\n  1389→\n  1390→    has_many :posts, Post\n  1391→  end\n  1392→\n  1393→  def changeset(user, attrs) do\n  1394→    user\n  1395→    |> cast(attrs, [:name, :email, :age])\n  1396→    |> validate_required([:name, :email])\n  1397→    |> validate_format(:email, ~r/@/)\n  1398→    |> validate_number(:age, greater_than: 0)\n  1399→    |> cast_embed(:profile, with: &profile_changeset/2)\n  1400→  end\n  1401→\n  1402→  defp profile_changeset(profile, attrs) do\n  1403→    profile\n  1404→    |> cast(attrs, [:bio, :skills])\n  1405→    |> validate_length(:bio, max: 500)\n  1406→  end\n  1407→end\n  1408→```\n  1409→\n  1410→### LiveView Form Handling\n  1411→\n  1412→```elixir\n  1413→defmodule MyAppWeb.UserFormLive do\n  1414→  use MyAppWeb, :live_view\n  1415→\n  1416→  def render(assigns) do\n  1417→    ~H\"\"\"\n  1418→    <div class=\"user-form\">\n  1419→      <h1>User Profile</h1>\n  1420→      <.vue form={@form} v-component=\"UserForm\" v-socket={@socket} />\n  1421→    </div>\n  1422→    \"\"\"\n  1423→  end\n  1424→\n  1425→  def mount(%{\"id\" => id}, _session, socket) do\n  1426→    user = Users.get_user!(id)\n  1427→    changeset = User.changeset(user, %{})\n  1428→\n  1429→    socket =\n  1430→      socket\n  1431→      |> assign(:user, user)\n  1432→      |> assign(:form, to_form(changeset, as: :user))\n  1433→\n  1434→    {:ok, socket}\n  1435→  end\n  1436→\n  1437→  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n  1438→    # New user\n  1439→    changeset = User.changeset(%User{}, %{})\n  1440→\n  1441→    socket =\n  1442→      socket\n  1443→      |> assign(:user, nil)\n  1444→      |> assign(:form, to_form(changeset, as: :user))\n  1445→\n  1446→    {:ok, socket}\n  1447→  end\n  1448→\n  1449→  def handle_event(\"validate\", %{\"user\" => user_params}, socket) do\n  1450→    user = socket.assigns.user || %User{}\n  1451→\n  1452→    changeset =\n  1453→      user\n  1454→      |> User.changeset(user_params)\n  1455→      # Setting :action is crucial - without it, the changeset won't expose errors.\n  1456→      # Ecto changesets only show errors when an action is set (like :validate, :insert, :update).\n  1457→      # This triggers error display in the Vue form without actually persisting data.\n  1458→      |> Map.put(:action, :validate)\n  1459→\n  1460→    {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\n  1461→  end\n  1462→\n  1463→  def handle_event(\"submit\", %{\"user\" => user_params}, socket) do\n  1464→    case save_user(socket.assigns.user, user_params) do\n  1465→      {:ok, user} ->\n  1466→        socket =\n  1467→          socket\n  1468→          |> put_flash(:info, \"User saved successfully!\")\n  1469→          |> redirect(to: ~p\"/users/#{user}\")\n  1470→\n  1471→        {:noreply, socket}\n  1472→\n  1473→      {:error, changeset} ->\n  1474→        {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\n  1475→    end\n  1476→  end\n  1477→\n  1478→  defp save_user(nil, user_params) do\n  1479→    %User{}\n  1480→    |> User.changeset(user_params)\n  1481→    |> Repo.insert()\n  1482→  end\n  1483→\n  1484→  defp save_user(user, user_params) do\n  1485→    user\n  1486→    |> User.changeset(user_params)\n  1487→    |> Repo.update()\n  1488→  end\n  1489→end\n  1490→```\n  1491→\n  1492→### Validation Best Practices\n  1493→\n  1494→```elixir\n  1495→# In your context module\n  1496→defmodule MyApp.Users do\n  1497→  def change_user(user \\\\ %User{}, attrs \\\\ %{}) do\n  1498→    User.changeset(user, attrs)\n  1499→  end\n  1500→\n  1501→  def create_user(attrs \\\\ %{}) do\n  1502→    %User{}\n  1503→    |> User.changeset(attrs)\n  1504→    |> Repo.insert()\n  1505→  end\n  1506→\n  1507→  def update_user(user, attrs) do\n  1508→    user\n  1509→    |> User.changeset(attrs)\n  1510→    |> Repo.update()\n  1511→  end\n  1512→\n  1513→  def validate_user_step(user, attrs, step) do\n  1514→    case step do\n  1515→      :basic_info ->\n  1516→        user\n  1517→        |> cast(attrs, [:name, :email])\n  1518→        |> validate_required([:name, :email])\n  1519→\n  1520→      :profile ->\n  1521→        user\n  1522→        |> cast_embed(:profile)\n  1523→\n  1524→      :complete ->\n  1525→        User.changeset(user, attrs)\n  1526→    end\n  1527→  end\n  1528→end\n  1529→```\n  1530→\n  1531→### Form Reset on Successful Submission\n  1532→\n  1533→By default, `useLiveForm` does not automatically reset form state after submission. This allows for flexible handling of different success scenarios (redirects, modals, etc.). However, you can opt into automatic form reset by returning `{:reply, %{reset: true}, socket}` from your submit event handler.\n  1534→\n  1535→#### Manual Form Management (Default Behavior)\n  1536→\n  1537→```elixir\n  1538→def handle_event(\"submit\", %{\"user\" => user_params}, socket) do\n  1539→  case save_user(socket.assigns.user, user_params) do\n  1540→    {:ok, user} ->\n  1541→      # Redirect after successful save\n  1542→      {:noreply, redirect(socket, to: ~p\"/users/#{user}\")}\n  1543→\n  1544→    {:error, changeset} ->\n  1545→      # Show validation errors\n  1546→      {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\n  1547→  end\n  1548→end\n  1549→```\n  1550→\n  1551→#### Automatic Form Reset\n  1552→\n  1553→When you want the form to reset after successful submission (useful for \"create another\" workflows or staying on the same page), use the `{:reply, %{reset: true}, socket}` pattern:\n  1554→\n  1555→```elixir\n  1556→def handle_event(\"submit\", %{\"contact\" => contact_params}, socket) do\n  1557→  case create_contact(contact_params) do\n  1558→    {:ok, contact} ->\n  1559→      socket =\n  1560→        socket\n  1561→        |> put_flash(:info, \"Contact created successfully!\")\n  1562→        |> assign(:form, to_form(Contact.changeset(%Contact{}, %{}), as: :contact))\n  1563→\n  1564→      # Tell the Vue component to reset form state\n  1565→      {:reply, %{reset: true}, socket}\n  1566→\n  1567→    {:error, changeset} ->\n  1568→      {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :contact))}\n  1569→  end\n  1570→end\n  1571→```\n  1572→\n  1573→#### What Gets Reset\n  1574→\n  1575→When `{reset: true}` is received, the Vue form component will:\n  1576→\n  1577→- Reset all field values to their current server state (from `form.values`)\n  1578→- Clear all touched states (`isTouched` becomes `false`)\n  1579→- Reset submit count to 0\n  1580→- Clear dirty states (`isDirty` becomes `false`)\n  1581→- Update `initialValues` to match current form values\n  1582→\n  1583→#### Multi-Step Form Reset\n  1584→\n  1585→For multi-step forms or complex workflows, you can conditionally reset:\n  1586→\n  1587→```elixir\n  1588→def handle_event(\"submit\", %{\"order\" => order_params}, socket) do\n  1589→  case create_order(order_params) do\n  1590→    {:ok, order} ->\n  1591→      socket = put_flash(socket, :info, \"Order created successfully!\")\n  1592→\n  1593→      case socket.assigns.action do\n  1594→        :create_another ->\n  1595→          # Reset form to create another order\n  1596→          socket = assign(socket, form: to_form(Order.changeset(%Order{}, %{}), as: :order))\n  1597→          {:reply, %{reset: true}, socket}\n  1598→\n  1599→        :checkout ->\n  1600→          # Redirect to checkout\n  1601→          {:noreply, redirect(socket, to: ~p\"/checkout/#{order}\")}\n  1602→\n  1603→        :view_order ->\n  1604→          # Redirect to order details\n  1605→          {:noreply, redirect(socket, to: ~p\"/orders/#{order}\")}\n  1606→      end\n  1607→\n  1608→    {:error, changeset} ->\n  1609→      {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :order))}\n  1610→  end\n  1611→end\n  1612→```\n  1613→\n  1614→#### Vue Component Handling\n  1615→\n  1616→The Vue component automatically handles the reset response:\n  1617→\n  1618→```html\n  1619→<script setup>\n  1620→const form = useLiveForm(() => props.form, {\n  1621→  submitEvent: 'submit'\n  1622→})\n  1623→\n  1624→const handleSubmit = async () => {\n  1625→  try {\n  1626→    const result = await form.submit()\n  1627→    \n  1628→    // If server returned {reset: true}, form is already reset\n  1629→    if (result?.reset) {\n  1630→      console.log('Form was reset after successful submission')\n  1631→    }\n  1632→    \n  1633→    // Additional success handling if needed\n  1634→  } catch (error) {\n  1635→    console.error('Submission failed:', error)\n  1636→  }\n  1637→}\n  1638→</script>\n  1639→```\n  1640→\n  1641→#### Best Practices\n  1642→\n  1643→1. **Use reset for \"create another\" workflows** where users typically want to submit multiple similar forms\n  1644→2. **Don't use reset when redirecting** - if you're redirecting after success, reset is unnecessary\n  1645→3. **Reset with fresh form data** - always assign a new form with fresh initial values before returning `{:reply, %{reset: true}, socket}`\n  1646→4. **Consider user experience** - reset only when it improves the user flow, not as a default behavior\n  1647→\n  1648→```elixir\n  1649→# Good: Reset for contact form that stays on same page\n  1650→def handle_event(\"submit\", %{\"contact\" => params}, socket) do\n  1651→  case MyApp.Contacts.create_contact(params) do\n  1652→    {:ok, _contact} ->\n  1653→      socket =\n  1654→        socket\n  1655→        |> put_flash(:info, \"Message sent successfully!\")\n  1656→        |> assign(:form, to_form(Contact.changeset(%Contact{}, %{}), as: :contact))\n  1657→      \n  1658→      {:reply, %{reset: true}, socket}\n  1659→      \n  1660→    {:error, changeset} ->\n  1661→      {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :contact))}\n  1662→  end\n  1663→end\n  1664→\n  1665→# Also good: No reset when redirecting\n  1666→def handle_event(\"submit\", %{\"user\" => params}, socket) do\n  1667→  case MyApp.Accounts.create_user(params) do\n  1668→    {:ok, user} ->\n  1669→      {:noreply, redirect(socket, to: ~p\"/users/#{user}\")}\n  1670→      \n  1671→    {:error, changeset} ->\n  1672→      {:noreply, assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :user))}\n  1673→  end\n  1674→end\n  1675→```\n  1676→\n  1677→## Complete Examples\n  1678→\n  1679→### Simple Contact Form\n  1680→\n  1681→A basic form demonstrating core concepts:\n  1682→\n  1683→```html\n  1684→<!-- ContactForm.vue -->\n  1685→<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n  1686→import { useLiveForm, type Form } from 'live_vue'\n  1687→\n  1688→type ContactForm = {\n  1689→  name: string\n  1690→  email: string\n  1691→  subject: string\n  1692→  message: string\n  1693→  contact_method: 'email' | 'phone'\n  1694→  phone?: string\n  1695→}\n  1696→\n  1697→const props = defineProps<{ form: Form<ContactForm> }>()\n  1698→\n  1699→const form = useLiveForm(() => props.form, {\n  1700→  changeEvent: 'validate',\n  1701→  submitEvent: 'submit',\n  1702→  debounceInMiliseconds: 200\n  1703→})\n  1704→\n  1705→const nameField = form.field('name')\n  1706→const emailField = form.field('email', { type: 'email' })\n  1707→const subjectField = form.field('subject')\n  1708→const messageField = form.field('message')\n  1709→// For radio buttons, create separate field instances with different values\n  1710→// The { type: 'radio', value: '...' } options ensure proper checked state binding\n  1711→const contactMethodEmail = form.field('contact_method', { type: 'radio', value: 'email' })\n  1712→const contactMethodPhone = form.field('contact_method', { type: 'radio', value: 'phone' })\n  1713→const phoneField = form.field('phone', { type: 'tel' })\n  1714→\n  1715→const needsPhone = computed(() =>\n  1716→  contactMethodEmail.value.value === 'phone'\n  1717→)\n  1718→\n  1719→const submitForm = async () => {\n  1720→  try {\n  1721→    await form.submit()\n  1722→    // Success feedback will be handled by LiveView\n  1723→  } catch (error) {\n  1724→    console.error('Submission failed:', error)\n  1725→  }\n  1726→}\n  1727→</script>\n  1728→\n  1729→<template>\n  1730→  <div class=\"contact-form\">\n  1731→    <h2>Contact Us</h2>\n  1732→\n  1733→    <div class=\"form-grid\">\n  1734→      <div class=\"field\">\n  1735→        <label :for=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Name *</label>\n  1736→        <input\n  1737→          v-bind=\"nameField.inputAttrs.value\"\n  1738→          :class=\"{ error: nameField.isTouched.value && nameField.errorMessage.value }\"\n  1739→        />\n  1740→        <div v-if=\"nameField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n  1741→          {{ nameField.errorMessage.value }}\n  1742→        </div>\n  1743→      </div>\n  1744→\n  1745→      <div class=\"field\">\n  1746→        <label :for=\"emailField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Email *</label>\n  1747→        <input\n  1748→          v-bind=\"emailField.inputAttrs.value\"\n  1749→          :class=\"{ error: emailField.isTouched.value && emailField.errorMessage.value }\"\n  1750→        />\n  1751→        <div v-if=\"emailField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n  1752→          {{ emailField.errorMessage.value }}\n  1753→        </div>\n  1754→      </div>\n  1755→    </div>\n  1756→\n  1757→    <div class=\"field\">\n  1758→      <label :for=\"subjectField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Subject *</label>\n  1759→      <input v-bind=\"subjectField.inputAttrs.value\" />\n  1760→      <div v-if=\"subjectField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n  1761→        {{ subjectField.errorMessage.value }}\n  1762→      </div>\n  1763→    </div>\n  1764→\n  1765→    <div class=\"field\">\n  1766→      <label>Preferred Contact Method</label>\n  1767→      <div class=\"radio-group\">\n  1768→        <label>\n  1769→          <!-- inputAttrs includes type=\"radio\", value=\"email\", checked state, and event handlers -->\n  1770→          <input v-bind=\"contactMethodEmail.inputAttrs.value\" />\n  1771→          Email\n  1772→        </label>\n  1773→        <label>\n  1774→          <input v-bind=\"contactMethodPhone.inputAttrs.value\" />\n  1775→          Phone\n  1776→        </label>\n  1777→      </div>\n  1778→    </div>\n  1779→\n  1780→    <div v-if=\"needsPhone\" class=\"field\">\n  1781→      <label :for=\"phoneField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Phone Number</label>\n  1782→      <input v-bind=\"phoneField.inputAttrs.value\" />\n  1783→      <div v-if=\"phoneField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n  1784→        {{ phoneField.errorMessage.value }}\n  1785→      </div>\n  1786→    </div>\n  1787→\n  1788→    <div class=\"field\">\n  1789→      <label :for=\"messageField.inputAttrs.value.id\">Message *</label>\n  1790→      <textarea\n  1791→        v-bind=\"messageField.inputAttrs.value\"\n  1792→        rows=\"5\"\n  1793→        :class=\"{ error: messageField.isTouched.value && messageField.errorMessage.value }\"\n  1794→      />\n  1795→      <div v-if=\"messageField.errorMessage.value\" class=\"error-message\">\n  1796→        {{ messageField.errorMessage.value }}\n  1797→      </div>\n  1798→    </div>\n  1799→\n  1800→    <div class=\"form-actions\">\n  1801→      <button @click=\"form.reset()\" type=\"button\" :disabled=\"!form.isDirty.value\">\n  1802→        Reset\n  1803→      </button>\n  1804→      <button @click=\"submitForm\" :disabled=\"!form.isValid.value || form.isValidating.value\" class=\"primary\">\n  1805→        {{ form.isValidating.value ? 'Validating...' : 'Send Message' }}\n  1806→      </button>\n  1807→    </div>\n  1808→\n  1809→    <div class=\"form-status\">\n  1810→      <small>\n  1811→        <span :class=\"{ valid: form.isValid.value, invalid: !form.isValid.value }\">\n  1812→          {{ form.isValid.value ? '✓' : '✗' }}\n  1813→        </span>\n  1814→        {{ form.isValidating.value ? 'Validating...' : form.isDirty.value ? 'Unsaved changes' : 'Form ready' }}\n  1815→      </small>\n  1816→    </div>\n  1817→  </div>\n  1818→</template>\n  1819→\n  1820→<style scoped>\n  1821→.contact-form {\n  1822→  max-width: 600px;\n  1823→  margin: 0 auto;\n  1824→  padding: 2rem;\n  1825→}\n  1826→\n  1827→.form-grid {\n  1828→  display: grid;\n  1829→  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n  1830→  gap: 1rem;\n  1831→}\n  1832→\n  1833→.field {\n  1834→  margin-bottom: 1rem;\n  1835→}\n  1836→\n  1837→.field label {\n  1838→  display: block;\n  1839→  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n  1840→  font-weight: 500;\n  1841→}\n  1842→\n  1843→.field input, .field textarea, .field select {\n  1844→  width: 100%;\n  1845→  padding: 0.75rem;\n  1846→  border: 1px solid #ccc;\n  1847→  border-radius: 4px;\n  1848→}\n  1849→\n  1850→.field input.error, .field textarea.error {\n  1851→  border-color: #e74c3c;\n  1852→}\n  1853→\n  1854→.radio-group {\n  1855→  display: flex;\n  1856→  gap: 1rem;\n  1857→}\n  1858→\n  1859→.radio-group label {\n  1860→  display: flex;\n  1861→  align-items: center;\n  1862→  gap: 0.5rem;\n  1863→  font-weight: normal;\n  1864→}\n  1865→\n  1866→.error-message {\n  1867→  color: #e74c3c;\n  1868→  font-size: 0.875rem;\n  1869→  margin-top: 0.25rem;\n  1870→}\n  1871→\n  1872→.form-actions {\n  1873→  display: flex;\n  1874→  gap: 1rem;\n  1875→  margin-top: 2rem;\n  1876→}\n  1877→\n  1878→.form-actions button {\n  1879→  padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;\n  1880→  border: none;\n  1881→  border-radius: 4px;\n  1882→  cursor: pointer;\n  1883→}\n  1884→\n  1885→.form-actions button:disabled {\n  1886→  opacity: 0.5;\n  1887→  cursor: not-allowed;\n  1888→}\n  1889→\n  1890→.form-actions button.primary {\n  1891→  background: #3498db;\n  1892→  color: white;\n  1893→}\n  1894→\n  1895→.form-status {\n  1896→  margin-top: 1rem;\n  1897→  text-align: center;\n  1898→}\n  1899→\n  1900→.valid { color: #27ae60; }\n  1901→.invalid { color: #e74c3c; }\n  1902→</style>\n  1903→```\n  1904→\n  1905→### Complex Nested Form\n  1906→\n  1907→An advanced form with nested objects, arrays, and dynamic fields can include:\n  1908→\n  1909→- Nested object fields (`owner.name`, `owner.email`)\n  1910→- Array fields with objects (`team_members[]`)\n  1911→- Deeply nested arrays (`tasks[].assignees[]`)\n  1912→- Dynamic field operations (add/remove/reorder)\n  1913→- Complex validation scenarios\n  1914→- Form state management\n  1915→\n  1916→See the patterns earlier in this guide for implementing each of these features, or explore interactive examples at [livevue.skalecki.dev](https://livevue.skalecki.dev).\n  1917→\n  1918→## Next Steps\n  1919→\n  1920→Now that you understand LiveVue forms, you might want to explore:\n  1921→\n  1922→- [Client-Side API](client_api.md) for detailed API reference and advanced patterns\n  1923→- [Testing](testing.md) for testing form components and validation logic\n  1924→- [Component Reference](component_reference.md) for LiveView-side form integration\n  1925→- [Basic Usage](basic_usage.md) for other LiveVue patterns and features\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R45EXfaLjZgcqByia7QETz","session_id":"64a1054d-d5d1-470b-988c-6d3926af5d5d","uuid":"06ad736e-4bb5-454b-b3af-5a336a54c1af"}
